34301.text:
{"condensed":"Applies incoming Pub/Sub (GCP) and NATS Streaming payment and auth events to shared registry databases, marking filings PAID and sending downstream messages to filer and emailer queues.

**Business-Pay (GCP payment flow):** POST with Bearer JWT to `/` receives `SimpleCloudEvent` (type `bc.registry.payment`); `verify_gcp_jwt` checks auth, fails return 403. `pay_filer.py` validates format and payment status. `Filing.get_filing_by_payment_token` finds filing; no match returns 404. Filing marked PAID with `payment_completion_date` and `payment_status_code="COMPLETED"`. `continuationIn` filings get staff Review; others go to filer queue if effective date reached. Emailer always gets `create_email_msg(PAID)`. **Entity-Pay (NATS):** `cb_subscription_handler` on `entity.filings` extracts token, checks `is_processable_message`, retries lookup 5×. COMPLETED→marked paid, published to emailer and filer (unless future-effective). TRANSACTION_FAILED leaves PENDING; other statuses raise `QueueException`. **Pay-Queue reconciliation:** POST to `/worker` verified by `external/gcp_auth.py`, dispatches on `ce.type` to payment/distribution/EFT reconciliation or temp ID update; handles NSF (freeze account, create invoice), publishes events. **Auth-Queue:** Pub/Sub push deduplicated by `message_id`, routed to name-events (auto-affiliation), activity-log, or pay-lock-unlock (org becomes NSF_SUSPENDED or ACTIVE, emails sent). 

GOTCHA: Nearly all workers catch all exceptions and still return 200 or ack; no redelivery. GOTCHA: Publishes to filer/emailer are swallowed after filing marked PAID—filing can be PAID but never filed or emailed, no retry or record. GOTCHA: Several tests pass without proving anything (activity log asserts True, timeouts swallowed, fixed test recipients).","defines":["POST /","POST /worker","bc.registry.payment","entity.filings","continuationIn","PAID","payment_status_code","payment_completion_date","TRANSACTION_FAILED","Review","NSF_SUSPENDED","ACTIVE","FilingMeta","QueueService","entity_queue_common","ServiceWorker"],"uses":[{"name":"verify_gcp_jwt","direction":"sends","what":"checks Bearer JWT from GCP Pub/Sub; failure returns 403"},{"name":"services/gcp_auth.py","direction":"reads","what":"GCP JWT verification module"},{"name":"external/gcp_auth.py","direction":"sends","what":"verifies GCP auth for /worker endpoint"},{"name":"pay_filer.py","direction":"reads","what":"validates message, cloud-event format, payment status, corp type; finds filing by payment token; marks filing PAID"},{"name":"Filing.get_filing_by_payment_token","direction":"sends","what":"looks up filing; returns 404 if not found"},{"name":"Filing.get_filing_by_payment_id","direction":"sends","what":"retrieves filing by payment ID, retried up to 5 times"},{"name":"create_filing_msg","direction":"sends","what":"publishes filing event to filer queue if effective date reached"},{"name":"create_email_msg","direction":"sends","what":"publishes to emailer queue with PAID option"},{"name":"filer queue","direction":"sends","what":"receives filing events; not sent for future-effective filings"},{"name":"emailer queue","direction":"sends","what":"receives email messages with PAID option"},{"name":"cb_subscription_handler","direction":"receives","what":"NATS message handler on entity.filings topic"},{"name":"is_processable_message","direction":"reads","what":"checks if message is processable"},{"name":"process_payment","direction":"reads","what":"marks COMPLETED payment as paid, publishes to emailer and filer"},{"name":"QueueException","direction":"sends","what":"raised for non-TRANSACTION_FAILED, non-COMPLETED statuses"},{"name":"resources/worker.py","direction":"reads","what":"dispatches on ce.type; dedupes by message_id"},{"name":"services/payment_reconciliations.py","direction":"reads","what":"handles NSF failures (freeze account, create invoice), credit records, account lookup; publishes payment events"},{"name":"process_name_events","direction":"reads","what":"handles auto-affiliation auth events"},{"name":"process_activity_log","direction":"reads","what":"processes activity log auth events"},{"name":"process_pay_lock_unlock_event","direction":"reads","what":"changes org to NSF_SUSPENDED or ACTIVE with mailer notification"},{"name":"reconcile_payments","direction":"reads","what":"reconciles payment events"},{"name":"reconcile_distributions","direction":"reads","what":"reconciles distribution events"},{"name":"reconcile_eft_payments","direction":"reads","what":"reconciles EFT payment events"},{"name":"update_temporary_identifier","direction":"reads","what":"updates temporary identifiers"}]}

34304.text:
{"condensed":"Architectural overview of the BC Registries pay and filing queue system, which creates and settles invoices, payments, refunds, routing slips, EFT credits and statements across PayBC/CFS, BCOL, Direct Pay, CGI and Notify API.

**Main flows:** (1) Pay-api validates and authorizes invoice requests, calls PaymentService, creates transactions, marks invoices PAID with receipts and publishes events. (2) Payment-jobs scheduled tasks create CFS/PAD accounts and push invoices to CFS; EJV, AP and CGI tasks build feeder files to MinIO/SFTP, marking invoices UPLOADED. (3) Reconciliation: POST to `/worker` verified by GCP auth; payment_reconciliations reads CAS files and sets invoices PAID/PARTIAL/COMPLETED; PAD failures freeze accounts and publish NSF; cgi_reconciliations sets invoice/disbursement/refund status; eft_reconciliation saves transactions, creates credits, applies pending payments. (4) EFT links start PENDING; apply_eft_credit processes them; refunds transition PENDING_REFUND to APPROVED/DECLINED. (5) Routing slips transition via RoutingSlipStatusTransitionService; RoutingSlipTask handles link/NSF/void/correction/adjust against CFS. (6) Payment-completed filing: Business-Pay and entity-Pay queues verify JWT (403 on fail), find filing by payment token (404 if none), set filing PAID, create Review for continuationIn, notify emailer; entity-Pay retries lookup 5x, failed transaction leaves filing PENDING. (7) Filing applied: future-effective-filings or legal API publishes filing ID to entity-filer; type handlers write rows; entity-emailer sends to notify API (tracker COMPLETE/FAILED); entity-bn sends CRA requests (BNException raised for redelivery, BNRetryExceededException after max retries); entity-digital-credentials replaces/revokes Traction credentials. (8) Auth-queue handles name-event auto-affiliation, activity logs, pay lock/unlock (sets org NSF_SUSPENDED or ACTIVE); account-mailer renders and sends deduplicated templates. (9) BCOL API picks apply-charge or debit-account by role and calls SOAP.

**GOTCHA: Swallowed errors.** Most workers, jobs and publishers catch broad exceptions and return 200 or ack; filing can be PAID but never filed or emailed; failed work not redelivered except DB errors, entity-bn exceptions, and Business-Pay's 403/404. **GOTCHA: Non-atomic multi-record writes.** complete_payment, EFT credit application, refunds, and CFS-then-DB steps commit separately; failure partway leaves half-updated state. **GOTCHA: Scheduling and idempotency.** StatementDueTask must run after StatementTask; date override silently disables notifications; future-effective job does not dedupe, can succeed while filing nothing.","defines":["pay-api REST invoice resource (v1)","PaymentService.create_invoice","PaymentSystemFactory.create","complete_post_invoice","PaymentTransaction","update_transaction","complete_payment","publish_status","payment-jobs scheduled tasks","CreateInvoiceTask","EjvPaymentTask","EjvPartnerDistributionTask","ApTask","/worker endpoint","gcp_auth","payment_reconciliations","cgi_reconciliations","eft_reconciliation","create_shortname_link","apply_eft_credit","link_electronic_funds_transfers_cfs","reverse_electronic_funds_transfers_cfs","RoutingSlipStatusTransitionService","RoutingSlipTask","FAS routing slip services (create, do_link, update)","bc.registry.payment cloud event","Business-Pay queue service","entity-Pay queue service","future-effective-filings job","entity_queue_common","entity-filer","process_filing","entity-emailer","send_email","entity-bn","request_bn_hub","entity-digital-credentials queue service","auth-queue","account-mailer","BCOL API POST /bcol"],"uses":[{"name":"pay-api JSON schemas and validation helper","direction":"reads","what":"Validates invoice request body against defined schemas"},{"name":"check_auth","direction":"receives","what":"Authorization check called before create_invoice; no condition shown"},{"name":"CFS/PAD accounts","direction":"sends","what":"Payment-jobs create and activate accounts"},{"name":"MinIO","direction":"sends","what":"CGI feeder files pushed before SFTP"},{"name":"SFTP","direction":"sends","what":"CGI feeder files sent from MinIO"},{"name":"CAS files","direction":"reads","what":"Reconciliation input; payment_reconciliations parses them"},{"name":"Notify API","direction":"sends","what":"entity-emailer posts {recipients, content} for email send"},{"name":"CRA (BN Hub) requests","direction":"sends","what":"entity-bn sends through request_bn_hub; raises BNException for redelivery, BNRetryExceededException after BN_HUB_MAX_RETRY"},{"name":"Traction","direction":"sends","what":"entity-digital-credentials replaces or revokes digital credentials"},{"name":"SOAP BCOL service","direction":"sends","what":"BCOL API calls apply-charge or debit-account based on role"},{"name":"Business database","direction":"sends","what":"Filing and event messages applied after payment or legal API publish"},{"name":"filer queue","direction":"sends","what":"Other filings published once effective"},{"name":"mailer consumer","direction":"sends","what":"Events published after filing applied"},{"name":"auth consumer","direction":"sends","what":"Events published after filing applied"},{"name":"payment consumer","direction":"sends","what":"Events published after filing applied"},{"name":"JWT verification","direction":"reads","what":"Business-Pay and entity-Pay verify JWT from cloud event; 403 on failure, no other check shown"},{"name":"payment token lookup","direction":"reads","what":"Filing found by payment token; 404 if none found"},{"name":"BN_HUB_MAX_RETRY","direction":"reads","what":"Config constant; exceeded triggers BNRetryExceededException"},{"name":"NSF_SUSPENDED, ACTIVE org states","direction":"sends","what":"auth-queue sets org state via pay lock/unlock"}]}

34344.text:
{"condensed":"Loads and maintains the dashboard state when this Vue component initializes, mounts, and unmounts by fetching business entity data, authorization checks, filing history, and tasks from external services, then storing results in Pinia stores.

Entry points: `created()` listens for 'reloadData' global events and clears task, pending, and filing lists before refetching; `mounted()` calls `fetchData()` only if `isAuthenticated` is true; `beforeUnmount()` stops listening. Main flow in `fetchData()`: sets loading flag false, fetches server date and stores as both JS Date and YYYY-MM-DD string, retrieves Keycloak JWT from sessionStorage and extracts roles, checks that `businessId` or `tempRegNumber` exists, calls `AuthServices.fetchAuthorizations()` with the relevant ID and throws if no auth role returned (decision: if authorization fails, shows auth error dialog and returns early without fetching remaining data), fetches user info and updates Launch Darkly, then branches: if `businessId` exists calls `fetchBusinessData()` which fetches entity info, business info, tasks, filings, and parties in parallel and throws if any missing, then calls `loadStateFiling()` and stores config object; if `tempRegNumber` exists fetches bootstrap filing and stores it, and if it is a todo with a NR number fetches and stores the NR data. If `businessId` exists also calls `fetchStoreAddressData()` which fetches addresses or handles 404 "not found" by storing null business office. Errors in business data branch log to console and Sentry, errors in bootstrap branch show invalid dialog. Entry points show no permission checks beyond the `isAuthenticated` guard in `mounted()`.

GOTCHA: authorization check throws if no role, but only logs the error—does not re-raise it or halt the app when user info or Launch Darkly fails. Address fetch catches 404 only if status is 404 AND URL includes 'addresses' AND message includes 'address not found'—other 404s throw. Bootstrap filing and NR data errors only log and show dialog; no retry or Sentry capture.","defines":[],"uses":[{"name":"reloadData","direction":"receives","what":"Global event emitted to this component's root; triggers data refresh"},{"name":"isAuthenticated","direction":"reads","what":"Boolean checked in mounted() to gate fetchData() call"},{"name":"businessId","direction":"reads","what":"Identifier checked in fetchData() to determine if entity is a business; sent to AuthServices.fetchAuthorizations, LegalServices.fetchTasks, loadFilings, LegalServices.fetchParties, LegalServices.fetchAddresses"},{"name":"tempRegNumber","direction":"reads","what":"Identifier checked in fetchData() as alternative to businessId; sent to AuthServices.fetchAuthorizations, loadFilings, LegalServices.fetchBootstrapFiling"},{"name":"getServerDate","direction":"sends","what":"Called to fetch current server date; result stored as JS Date and YYYY-MM-DD string"},{"name":"getJWT","direction":"sends","what":"Retrieves Keycloak JWT from sessionStorage with key SessionStorageKeys.KeyCloakToken, decodes and returns parsed token object"},{"name":"SessionStorageKeys.KeyCloakToken","direction":"reads","what":"Key in sessionStorage holding Keycloak token"},{"name":"fetchKeycloakRoles","direction":"sends","what":"Extracts roles array from JWT; throws if empty"},{"name":"AuthServices.fetchAuthorizations","direction":"sends","what":"Called with getAuthApiUrl and businessId or tempRegNumber; returns response with roles array that is checked for non-empty and stored"},{"name":"getAuthApiUrl","direction":"reads","what":"Endpoint URL sent to AuthServices.fetchAuthorizations and fetchUserInfo"},{"name":"storeAuthorizations","direction":"sends","what":"Processes response and stores auth roles or throws if none"},{"name":"AuthServices.fetchUserInfo","direction":"sends","what":"Called with getAuthApiUrl; returns userInfo with keycloakGuid, email, firstname, lastname, username"},{"name":"updateLaunchDarkly","direction":"sends","what":"Called with userInfo to update Launch Darkly user profile"},{"name":"UpdateLdUser","direction":"sends","what":"External Launch Darkly call with key (username), email, firstName, lastName, custom object containing Keycloak roles"},{"name":"fetchBusinessData","direction":"sends","what":"Calls AuthServices.fetchEntityInfo, loadBusinessInfo, LegalServices.fetchTasks, loadFilings, LegalServices.fetchParties in parallel; throws if any missing"},{"name":"AuthServices.fetchEntityInfo","direction":"sends","what":"Called with getAuthApiUrl and businessId"},{"name":"loadBusinessInfo","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useBusinessStore"},{"name":"LegalServices.fetchTasks","direction":"sends","what":"Called with businessId"},{"name":"loadFilings","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useFilingHistoryListStore called with businessId or tempRegNumber"},{"name":"LegalServices.fetchParties","direction":"sends","what":"Called with businessId"},{"name":"storeEntityInfo","direction":"sends","what":"Processes entity info response from AuthServices"},{"name":"storeTasks","direction":"sends","what":"Processes tasks response from LegalServices"},{"name":"storeParties","direction":"sends","what":"Processes parties response from LegalServices"},{"name":"loadStateFiling","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore called after business info loaded"},{"name":"storeConfigObject","direction":"sends","what":"Stores config object now that entity type is known"},{"name":"fetchStoreAddressData","direction":"sends","what":"Fetches business addresses; called after fetchBusinessData"},{"name":"LegalServices.fetchAddresses","direction":"sends","what":"Called with businessId; returns address data or throws 404 if address not found"},{"name":"storeAddresses","direction":"sends","what":"Stores address data or null business office on 404"},{"name":"LegalServices.fetchBootstrapFiling","direction":"sends","what":"Called with tempRegNumber; returns bootstrap filing/todo item"},{"name":"storeBootstrapItem","direction":"sends","what":"Processes bootstrap filing response"},{"name":"isBootstrapTodo","direction":"reads","what":"Boolean checked to conditionally fetch NR if bootstrap item is a todo"},{"name":"localNrNumber","direction":"reads","what":"NR number checked and sent to LegalServices.fetchNameRequest if present"},{"name":"LegalServices.fetchNameRequest","direction":"sends","what":"Called with localNrNumber if bootstrap is todo"},{"name":"storeNrData","direction":"sends","what":"Stores NR data and response together"},{"name":"Sentry.captureException","direction":"sends","what":"Called with error when business data fetch fails"},{"name":"businessAuthErrorDialog","direction":"sends","what":"Set to true if authorization fails and businessId exists"},{"name":"nameRequestAuthErrorDialog","direction":"sends","what":"Set to true if authorization fails and tempRegNumber exists"},{"name":"dashboardUnavailableDialog","direction":"sends","what":"Set to true if business data fetch throws"},{"name":"nameRequestInvalidDialog","direction":"sends","what":"Set to true if bootstrap filing fetch throws"},{"name":"nameRequestInvalidType","direction":"sends","what":"Set to null before bootstrap fetch"},{"name":"dateToPacificDateTime","direction":"sends","what":"Formats JS date for logging"},{"name":"dateToYyyyMmDd","direction":"sends","what":"Formats JS date to YYYY-MM-DD string"},{"name":"isVitestRunning","direction":"reads","what":"Checked to conditionally suppress console log"},{"name":"getKeycloakRoles","direction":"reads","what":"Read from store and passed to Launch Darkly custom object"},{"name":"setTasks","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; called with empty array on reload"},{"name":"setPendingsList","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; called with empty array on reload"},{"name":"setFilings","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useFilingHistoryListStore; called with empty array on reload"},{"name":"setCurrentJsDate","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; stores server date as JS Date"},{"name":"setCurrentDate","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; stores server date as YYYY-MM-DD string"},{"name":"setKeycloakRoles","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; stores roles array from JWT"},{"name":"setAuthRoles","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; stores roles from authorization response"},{"name":"setUserInfo","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; stores user info object"},{"name":"setUserKeycloakGuid","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; stores keycloakGuid from userInfo"},{"name":"setBootstrapFilingStatus","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; part of bootstrap storage"},{"name":"setBootstrapFilingType","direction":"sends","what":"Pinia action from useRootStore; part of bootstrap storage"}]}

35895.text:
{"condensed":"Component processors for Legal Filing entities: creates and updates Address, Office, Party, PartyRole (with role mapping), ShareClass, ShareSeries, Comment, and Filing User records. Takes structured JSON input (officer, address, role, share, and corporate comment data) and constructs or modifies ORM model instances.

Entry points: all functions are public methods callable from filing processors; this chunk shows no caller authorization checks. Receives `address_info` dict with streetAddress, streetAddressAdditional, addressCity, addressRegion, addressCountry, postalCode, deliveryInstructions; converts country name to ISO-2 alpha code via pycountry.countries.search_fuzzy(). Creates Address with address_type derived by stripping 'Address' suffix. `update_address()` overwrites all fields on an existing Address. `create_office()` loops addresses dict, creates Address for each key (used as type), appends to office.addresses. `create_party()` optionally searches existing Party by name/middle_initial/org_name via PartyRole.find_party_by_name(); if not found, constructs Party with firstName, lastName, middleInitial, title, organizationName (all uppercased), email, identifier, partyType, then attaches delivery and mailing Address objects and sets skip_party_listener=True. `create_role()` maps roleType via JSON_ROLE_CONVERTER dict (custodian→CUSTODIAN, completing party→COMPLETING_PARTY, director→DIRECTOR, incorporator→INCORPORATOR, proprietor→PROPRIETOR, partner→PARTNER) and creates PartyRole with appointment/cessation dates. `update_director()` overwrites director party name/title/addresses and cessation_date. `create_share_class()` constructs ShareClass with name, priority, max flags/values, par flags/values, currency, special_rights_flag; loops series array and appends ShareSeries to share_class.series. `create_comments()` iterates corp_comments array, creates Comment per entry with business_id, comment text (cc_comments), timestamp (cc_comment_dts_pacific). `update_filing_user()` retrieves User by username via User.find_by_username(); if found, sets filing_submission.submitter_id; else creates new User with username, firstname, lastname, middlename, email, creation_date and assigns to filing_submission.filing_submitter.

GOTCHA: `pycountry.countries.search_fuzzy()` is not wrapped in error handling; will raise if country name is invalid or ambiguous. `create_party()` with create=True searches by name but does not guard against finding the wrong person. `update_director()` assumes delivery_address exists but checks mailing_address; if deliveryAddress key is missing from new_info, overwrites with None.","defines":["create_address","update_address","create_office","create_party","create_role","update_director","create_share_class","create_comments","update_filing_user","JSON_ROLE_CONVERTER"],"uses":[{"name":"Address","direction":"sends","what":"constructs and modifies Address ORM model with street, city, region, country (ISO-2 alpha), postal_code, delivery_instructions, address_type"},{"name":"pycountry.countries.search_fuzzy","direction":"sends","what":"looks up country name and returns alpha_2 code; no error handling shown"},{"name":"Office","direction":"sends","what":"constructs Office ORM model with office_type and addresses list"},{"name":"Business","direction":"receives","what":"filtering and data source; business.id used to link Address, Party, Comment"},{"name":"Party","direction":"sends","what":"constructs and modifies Party ORM model with first_name, last_name, middle_initial, title, organization_name, email, identifier, party_type, delivery_address, mailing_address"},{"name":"PartyRole.find_party_by_name","direction":"sends","what":"searches existing Party by business_id, first_name, last_name, middle_initial, org_name; no check on result uniqueness shown"},{"name":"PartyRole","direction":"sends","what":"constructs PartyRole ORM model with role (from JSON_ROLE_CONVERTER), appointment_date, cessation_date, party reference"},{"name":"ShareClass","direction":"sends","what":"constructs ShareClass ORM model with name, priority, max_share_flag, max_shares, par_value_flag, par_value, currency, special_rights_flag"},{"name":"ShareSeries","direction":"sends","what":"constructs ShareSeries ORM model with name, priority, max_share_flag, max_shares, special_rights_flag; appended to share_class.series"},{"name":"Comment","direction":"sends","what":"constructs Comment ORM model with business_id, comment text, timestamp (cc_comment_dts_pacific)"},{"name":"User.find_by_username","direction":"sends","what":"retrieves User by username; returns None if not found"},{"name":"User","direction":"sends","what":"constructs User ORM model with username, firstname, lastname, middlename, email, creation_date"},{"name":"Filing","direction":"receives","what":"reference parameter; submitter_id or filing_submitter field is updated"}]}

35899.text:
{"condensed":"Applies a correction filing to a business and its parties in a legal filing system. Entry point `correct_business_data` is called by a correction filing processor with no visible permission check; updates business legal name, NAICS code, office addresses, parties, court order, and start date from a correction filing JSON. Extracts values from nested correction filing paths using dpath.util.get, suppressing IndexError/KeyError/TypeError for missing fields. If legal name differs, logs old and new names in filing_meta.correction. If NAICS differs, updates via business_info.update_naics_info and logs change. For business office addresses with an id, updates via update_address; otherwise creates via create_address. Calls update_parties to handle party changes. Updates court order via filings.update_filing_court_order if present. Converts start_date string to datetime, adds 8-hour offset, assigns to business.start_date.

update_parties ceases party roles not in the incoming party list by setting cessation_date to now, then creates or updates each party. Existing int ids trigger update via _update_party; missing or string UUID ids trigger create via _create_party_info. _update_party looks up Party by id, updates all fields (first_name, last_name, middle_initial, title, organization_name, party_type, email, identifier) with uppercase/lowercase normalization, then updates or creates delivery and mailing addresses. _create_party_info creates a new party, creates a PartyRole for each role type with appointment/cessation dates, appends to correction_filing_rec.filing_party_roles if role is COMPLETING_PARTY, otherwise to business.party_roles.

GOTCHA: suppressed exceptions hide missing or malformed JSON silently; no validation that corrections are logically sound or permitted. No check that party updates don't violate role constraints.","defines":["correct_business_data","update_parties"],"uses":[{"name":"dpath.util.get","direction":"sends","what":"Extracts nested dictionary values from correction filing JSON by path string."},{"name":"Business.legal_name","direction":"sends","what":"Sets business legal name from nameRequest in correction filing."},{"name":"business_info.update_naics_info","direction":"sends","what":"Updates NAICS code and description on business object from naics dict in correction filing."},{"name":"Address.find_by_id","direction":"sends","what":"Retrieves address by id to update in correction filing, no check shown for access."},{"name":"update_address","direction":"sends","what":"Updates address fields from correction filing JSON for business office or party addresses."},{"name":"create_address","direction":"sends","what":"Creates new address with address_type (businessOffice, DELIVERY, MAILING) from correction filing JSON."},{"name":"filings.update_filing_court_order","direction":"sends","what":"Updates court order on correction filing record from courtOrder in correction filing JSON."},{"name":"PartyRole.get_party_roles","direction":"sends","what":"Retrieves all active party roles for business by id and date, to identify roles to cease."},{"name":"Party.find_by_id","direction":"sends","what":"Retrieves party by id for update; no check shown for access."},{"name":"create_party","direction":"sends","what":"Creates new party from party_info dict with business_id; create=False passed."},{"name":"create_role","direction":"sends","what":"Creates PartyRole with roleType (lowercased), appointmentDate, cessationDate."},{"name":"PartyRole.RoleTypes.COMPLETING_PARTY","direction":"reads","what":"Constant used to determine whether new role appends to filing_party_roles or business.party_roles."},{"name":"datetime.datetime","direction":"sends","what":"Parses ISO format start_date and gets current UTC time for party role cessation."}]}

36496.text:
{"condensed":"Scheduled job that advances involuntary business dissolution through three warning and notification stages. Entry point `run()` is called by the scheduler if the `enable-involuntary-dissolution` feature flag is on and cron schedules from configuration allow it. It reads cron expressions from `DISSOLUTIONS_STAGE_1_SCHEDULE`, `DISSOLUTIONS_STAGE_2_SCHEDULE`, `DISSOLUTIONS_STAGE_3_SCHEDULE` config keys to decide which stages execute today.

Stage 1 (not shown) processes batches. Stage 2 finds `BatchProcessing` rows in `PROCESSING` status at `WARNING_LEVEL_1` step whose `trigger_date` has passed, checks that email or letter `Furnishing` with status `PROCESSED` exists for the business, then either advances to `WARNING_LEVEL_2` step and sets `trigger_date` forward by `STAGE_2_DELAY` days, or marks the `BatchProcessing` `WITHDRAWN` with note 'Moved back into good standing' if business eligibility check fails. Stage 3 finds rows at `WARNING_LEVEL_2` step whose trigger date has passed, checks that gazette `Furnishing` with status `PROCESSED` exists, then either calls `create_invountary_dissolution_filing()` to make a filing, saves its ID, transitions to `DISSOLUTION` step and `QUEUED` status, and sends the filing ID to queue via `put_filing_on_queue()`, or marks `WITHDRAWN`. Both stages call `InvoluntaryDissolutionService.check_business_eligibility()` with `exclude_in_dissolution=False`, log decisions, and set `last_modified` timestamp. Stage 3 also calls `mark_eligible_batches_completed()` at the end. No check enforces who may call `run()`. TODO comments note missing checks that warnings were actually sent before advancing stages.

GOTCHA: no credential mechanism visible for queue write in stage 3; no transactional guarantee that `filing` creation and queue publish succeed together; broad exception catch logs and re-raises without retry.","defines":["run","stage_2_process","stage_3_process","check_run_schedule","can_run_today"],"uses":[{"name":"flags.is_on","direction":"reads","what":"Feature flag `enable-involuntary-dissolution` to gate entire job execution."},{"name":"Configuration.find_by_name","direction":"reads","what":"Configuration rows with names `DISSOLUTIONS_STAGE_1_SCHEDULE`, `DISSOLUTIONS_STAGE_2_SCHEDULE`, `DISSOLUTIONS_STAGE_3_SCHEDULE` returning cron expression strings in val field."},{"name":"croniter.match","direction":"reads","what":"External cron expression validator; determines if cron string matches today's date in US/Pacific timezone."},{"name":"BatchProcessing table","direction":"reads","what":"Rows with batch_id, status `PROCESSING`, step `WARNING_LEVEL_1` or `WARNING_LEVEL_2`, trigger_date <= now; filters by Batch.batch_type `INVOLUNTARY_DISSOLUTION` and Batch.status `PROCESSING`."},{"name":"Furnishing.find_by","direction":"reads","what":"Furnishing rows by batch_id and business_id; stage 2 filters for email or mail type with status `PROCESSED`, stage 3 filters for gazette type with status `PROCESSED`."},{"name":"InvoluntaryDissolutionService.check_business_eligibility","direction":"sends","what":"Called with business_identifier and EligibilityFilters(exclude_in_dissolution=False); returns eligibility boolean and second value (unused)."},{"name":"create_invountary_dissolution_filing","direction":"sends","what":"Called with business_id in stage 3; creates and returns a filing object with id field."},{"name":"put_filing_on_queue","direction":"sends","what":"Called with filing.id, application, and QueueService in stage 3 to enqueue filing for processing."},{"name":"mark_eligible_batches_completed","direction":"sends","what":"Called at end of stage 3 to mark batches complete when all associated batch_processings are completed."},{"name":"BatchProcessing.save","direction":"sends","what":"Writes BatchProcessing row updates (status, step, trigger_date, notes, filing_id, last_modified) to database."},{"name":"create_app","direction":"sends","what":"Creates Flask application context if none provided; used in main block."},{"name":"QueueService","direction":"receives","what":"Instantiated with Flask app and event loop; passed to stage_3_process and put_filing_on_queue."}]}

36988.text:
{"condensed":"Provides decorators to guard Flask route handlers with Traction authentication and digital credential access checks.

`requires_traction_auth` ensures a valid JWT token exists for Traction API calls, refreshing it if expired. It reads `TRACTION_API_URL`, `TRACTION_TENANT_ID`, and `TRACTION_API_KEY` from config; if missing, raises `EnvironmentError`. It checks if `current_app.api_token` exists and decodes it without signature verification. If the token is missing or its `exp` timestamp is at or before current UTC time, it POSTs to `{traction_api_url}/multitenancy/tenant/{traction_tenant_id}/token` with header `Content-Type: application/json` and body `{"api_key": traction_api_key}`. On success, saves `response.json()['token']` to `current_app.api_token`; on failure, `raise_for_status()` propagates the HTTP error. This chunk shows no caller check.

`can_access_digital_credentials` guards routes requiring digital credential access. It extracts `identifier` from kwargs, calls `Business.find_by_identifier(identifier)`, and returns `{"message": "{identifier} not found."}` with status 404 if not found. It then calls `are_digital_credentials_allowed(business, jwt)` and returns `{"message": "digital credential not available for: {identifier}."}` with status 401 if false. Only if both pass does it call the wrapped function. This chunk shows no caller check.","defines":["requires_traction_auth","can_access_digital_credentials"],"uses":[{"name":"current_app.config['TRACTION_API_URL']","direction":"reads","what":"Flask config key for Traction API base URL; decorator raises EnvironmentError if not set."},{"name":"current_app.config['TRACTION_TENANT_ID']","direction":"reads","what":"Flask config key for Traction tenant ID; decorator raises EnvironmentError if not set."},{"name":"current_app.config['TRACTION_API_KEY']","direction":"reads","what":"Flask config key for Traction API key; decorator raises EnvironmentError if not set."},{"name":"current_app.api_token","direction":"reads","what":"Flask app attribute holding cached JWT token for Traction; checked for existence and validity."},{"name":"current_app.api_token","direction":"sends","what":"Flask app attribute; decorator stores new token from Traction response."},{"name":"current_app.logger.info","direction":"sends","what":"Log message when JWT token expired or missing."},{"name":"requests.post","direction":"sends","what":"HTTP POST to Traction endpoint with Content-Type application/json and JSON body {"api_key": traction_api_key}; raises on HTTP error."},{"name":"pyjwt.decode","direction":"sends","what":"Decode JWT without signature verification; raises ExpiredSignatureError if token missing or exp timestamp at or before current UTC."},{"name":"Business.find_by_identifier","direction":"sends","what":"Lookup business by identifier string; returns None if not found."},{"name":"are_digital_credentials_allowed","direction":"sends","what":"Check if business has digital credential access; receives business object and jwt object."},{"name":"jwt","direction":"reads","what":"JWT object passed to are_digital_credentials_allowed for credential access check."}]}

37041.text:
{"condensed":"Stores and retrieves NAICS (North American Industry Classification System) business structure records at a specific hierarchical level and version.

Immutable database table with UUID primary key (naics_key), indexed by code, year, version, level, and class_title. Each record holds a six-digit code, year, version, hierarchical_structure string, class_title (up to 150 chars), class_definition (up to 5100 chars), optional superscript, and one-to-many relationship to NaicsElement records.

Entry points: find_by_search_term (searches by text across class_title and linked element descriptions), find_by_code (retrieves by code and level, defaulting to level 5), find_by_naics_key (retrieves by UUID). No permission checks shown. find_by_search_term branches on has_exact_match_class_title_match: if true, runs get_exact_match_query which returns all examples for matching titles or only matching examples for non-matching titles; if false, runs get_non_exact_match_query which splits search_term by space and matches each word against element_description. Both queries filter to current NAICS_YEAR and NAICS_VERSION from config, level 5, and element_type in [ALL_EXAMPLES, ILLUSTRATIVE_EXAMPLES]. json property returns dict with naicsKey, code, year, version, classTitle, classDefinition, and nested naicsElements array. get_naics_config reads NAICS_YEAR and NAICS_VERSION integers from app config.","defines":["NaicsStructure","naics_structures","find_by_search_term","find_by_code","find_by_naics_key","has_exact_match_class_title_match","get_exact_match_query","get_non_exact_match_query","get_naics_config","json"],"uses":[{"name":"db.Model","direction":"receives","what":"Base class for SQLAlchemy ORM model"},{"name":"NaicsElement","direction":"receives","what":"Related model joined in queries to filter by element_type (ALL_EXAMPLES, ILLUSTRATIVE_EXAMPLES) and element_description; no check on element access shown"},{"name":"current_app.config","direction":"reads","what":"Application configuration keys NAICS_YEAR and NAICS_VERSION as integers to filter all queries"},{"name":"db.session.query","direction":"sends","what":"SQLAlchemy queries executed with filters, joins, outer joins, contains_eager, and distinct for search and lookup operations"}]}

37194.text:
{"condensed":"Validates a Change of Directors filing for a business by checking director addresses and effective date against incorporation date, prior filings, and current time.

Entry point: `validate(business, cod)` takes a Business object and filing dictionary, returns an Error if invalid or None if valid; this chunk shows no caller check. Collects errors from two validators: `validate_directors_addresses()` checks that each director's address contains a valid ISO-2 country code via `pycountry.countries.search_fuzzy(country)[0].alpha_2`, appending error with path `/filing/changeOfDirectors/directors/{idx}/{address_type}/addressCountry` on LookupError. `validate_effective_date()` parses the `filing/header/effectiveDate` ISO string, converts to UTC datetime, then to legislation timezone date, and verifies: not in future (compares `datetime.utcnow()`), not before `business.founding_date`, and not before the most recent prior Change of Directors filing retrieved via `Filing.get_most_recent_legal_filing(business.id, Filing.FILINGS['changeOfDirectors']['name'])`. Each violation appends a distinct error message. Returns all accumulated errors as HTTPStatus.BAD_REQUEST with message list, or None.

GOTCHA: `validate_effective_date()` returns a dict on missing effective date but a list otherwise, breaking type consistency.","defines":["validate","validate_directors_addresses","validate_effective_date"],"uses":[{"name":"pycountry.countries.search_fuzzy","direction":"sends","what":"Called with country string; returns fuzzy-matched country object with alpha_2 attribute or raises LookupError."},{"name":"Filing.get_most_recent_legal_filing","direction":"sends","what":"Called with business.id and Filing.FILINGS['changeOfDirectors']['name']; returns Filing object or None."},{"name":"LegislationDatetime.as_legislation_timezone","direction":"sends","what":"Called with datetime object; returns datetime in legislation timezone."},{"name":"Error","direction":"sends","what":"Called with HTTPStatus.BAD_REQUEST and error message list to return."},{"name":"Address.JSON_ADDRESS_TYPES","direction":"reads","what":"List of address type keys to iterate over in director objects."},{"name":"datetime.utcnow","direction":"sends","what":"Called to get current UTC time for future date check."},{"name":"datetime.fromisoformat","direction":"sends","what":"Called with effective_datetime_str to parse ISO format string; raises ValueError on invalid format."},{"name":"babel","direction":"sends","what":"Called with error message strings for i18n translation."}]}

37220.text:
{"condensed":"Helper functions that return SQLAlchemy filter clauses for business eligibility checks in a dissolution-related system.

Four fixed checks: `_has_future_effective_filing()` queries for pending or paid filings against the business, returning True if any exist. `_has_delay_of_dissolution_filing()` is unimplemented and always returns False. `_is_limited_restored()` checks if the business has a non-null restoration expiry date not yet passed (UTC timezone). `_is_xpro_from_nwpta()` checks if the business is extraprovincial from NWPTA jurisdictions (legal type EXTRA_PRO_A, Canada, foreign region in AB/SK/MB).

`_check_feature_flags_filter()` gates on the flag `enable-involuntary-dissolution-filter`. If off, returns True (no filter). If on, reads `involuntary-dissolution-filter` config (include-accounts and exclude-accounts lists). Calls `_get_filtered_entities()` on each account ID to fetch affiliations via `AccountService.get_affiliations()`, extracting business identifiers (excluding those starting with T or NR). Returns SQLAlchemy clauses: if only exclude list, excludes those identifiers; if only include list, includes those; if both, includes from the include list minus overlap with exclude. `_get_filtered_entities()` loops account IDs, fetches entity affiliations, filters by identifier pattern, returns the list. No checks enforce who calls these helpers. Filing queries and restoration date checks use UTC timezone function.","defines":["_has_future_effective_filing","_has_delay_of_dissolution_filing","_is_limited_restored","_is_xpro_from_nwpta","_check_feature_flags_filter","_get_filtered_entities"],"uses":[{"name":"db.session.query","direction":"sends","what":"Queries Filing table filtered by business_id and status (PENDING or PAID)."},{"name":"Business","direction":"reads","what":"Table: reads id, legal_type, jurisdiction, foreign_jurisdiction_region, restoration_expiry_date columns."},{"name":"Filing","direction":"reads","what":"Table: reads business_id and _status columns."},{"name":"flags.is_on","direction":"reads","what":"Checks if feature flag 'enable-involuntary-dissolution-filter' is enabled."},{"name":"flags.value","direction":"reads","what":"Reads config dict 'involuntary-dissolution-filter' with include-accounts and exclude-accounts keys."},{"name":"AccountService.get_affiliations","direction":"sends","what":"Calls with org_id (int) to fetch list of entity dicts; each dict contains businessIdentifier field."},{"name":"func.timezone","direction":"reads","what":"SQLAlchemy function to apply UTC timezone in database query."},{"name":"func.now","direction":"reads","what":"SQLAlchemy function to get current timestamp in database query."}]}

38533.text:
{"condensed":"Builds and sends email notification when an Affiliation filing is created or modified in BCRegistry.

Entry point: `process(email_info, token)` is called by an external handler with filing data and authorization token; this chunk shows no permission check. Retrieves filing details (type, status, effective date) by `get_filing_info()` via filingId from email_info. Reads template `BC-ALT-DRAFT.html` from `TEMPLATE_PATH` config, substitutes parts, and renders via Jinja2 with filing, business, header, dates, and dashboard URL built from `DASHBOARD_URL` config plus business identifier. Extracts recipients via `get_recipients(status, filing_json, token)`; if empty, returns empty dict. Constructs email with subject line `{legalName} - How to use BCRegistry.ca`, sender `BCRegistries@gov.bc.ca`, and rendered HTML body. Filing type display name is formatted by uppercasing first letter and splitting camelCase. Returns dict with recipients, requestBy, and content (subject and body).

GOTCHA: If `get_recipients()` returns empty, process returns empty dict instead of raising or logging the condition.","defines":["process"],"uses":[{"name":"get_filing_info","direction":"sends","what":"Called with filingId extracted from email_info; returns filing object, business data, and timezone-aware filing and effective dates."},{"name":"get_recipients","direction":"sends","what":"Called with status, filing_json, and token; returns list of recipient email addresses or falsy value; token used for authorization."},{"name":"substitute_template_parts","direction":"sends","what":"Called with template content; returns modified template string."},{"name":"TEMPLATE_PATH","direction":"reads","what":"Config key for directory path; chunk reads `BC-ALT-DRAFT.html` template from here."},{"name":"DASHBOARD_URL","direction":"reads","what":"Config key for base URL; chunk appends business identifier to build entity dashboard link."},{"name":"logger.debug","direction":"sends","what":"Logs filing_notification data at debug level."},{"name":"Template","direction":"sends","what":"Jinja2 template object; instantiated with autoescape=True and rendered with business, filing, header, dates, URLs, and filing_type."}]}

38535.text:
{"condensed":"Builds an email notification for an AGM Location Change filing in the business registry.

Entry point: `process(email_info, token)` receives an email info dict with `type`, `option` (status), and `filingId`; this chunk shows no check. Calls `get_filing_info` to fetch the filing, business, and localized dates. Loads an HTML template from `TEMPLATE_PATH/AGM-LOCCHG-{status}.html`, substitutes parts, and renders it via Jinja2 with business, filing, header, dates, dashboard URL, and filing type. Fetches PDF attachments via `_get_pdfs`: requests a filing PDF (type `letterOfAgmLocationChange`) via `get_filing_document`; if present, appends it as "Letter of AGM Location Change Approval.pdf". Posts to PAY_API_URL with the payment token to generate a receipt PDF, passing corpName, filingDateTime, effectiveDateTime (empty if same as filing date), filingIdentifier, and businessNumber (tax_id or empty); logs error if status is not 201, else appends receipt as "Receipt.pdf". Deduplicates recipients from `get_recipient_from_auth`, joins them comma-separated. Returns a dict with recipients, requestBy (hardcoded "BCRegistries@gov.bc.ca"), and content holding subject (formatted as "{legal name} - AGM Location Change Documents from the Business Registry" or "Numbered Company" if name starts with identifier), body (HTML), and attachments (PDF list ordered by attachOrder).

GOTCHA: Receipt generation returns only a logged error on failure; the email proceeds without it. GOTCHA: effectiveDateTime is omitted from the receipt request (sent as empty string) when it equals filingDateTime, which may create inconsistency if a consumer expects the field.","defines":["process"],"uses":[{"name":"get_filing_info","direction":"sends","what":"Called with filingId; returns filing, business dict, and localized filing and effective dates."},{"name":"TEMPLATE_PATH config","direction":"reads","what":"Reads HTML template file from TEMPLATE_PATH/AGM-LOCCHG-{status}.html."},{"name":"substitute_template_parts","direction":"sends","what":"Called with template string; returns template with parts substituted."},{"name":"get_filing_document","direction":"sends","what":"Called with business identifier, filing id, filing_pdf_type 'letterOfAgmLocationChange', and token; returns base64-encoded PDF or falsy."},{"name":"PAY_API_URL","direction":"sends","what":"Posts to PAY_API_URL/{payment_token}/receipts with Authorization Bearer token header, requesting receipt PDF with corpName, filingDateTime, effectiveDateTime, filingIdentifier, businessNumber; expects status 201."},{"name":"Business.find_by_internal_id","direction":"sends","what":"Called with filing.business_id; returns business object or None to extract tax_id."},{"name":"get_recipient_from_auth","direction":"sends","what":"Called with business identifier and token; returns recipient email address or None."},{"name":"DASHBOARD_URL config","direction":"reads","what":"Reads URL base for entity dashboard link."},{"name":"logger","direction":"sends","what":"Logs debug and error messages."}]}

38536.text:
{"condensed":"Builds and returns an email notification for an amalgamation filing event in the legal entity system.

Entry point: `process(email_info, token)` receives calls from the email notification workflow; this chunk shows no check. Takes filing ID from email_info, retrieves the filing record and business details. For PAID status, uses the temporary registration number and retrieves the primary or holding business legal name from filing data. For COMPLETED status, uses stored business data. Renders an HTML email template with filing details, filing date, effective date, business info, entity dashboard URL, and filing type. Calls `_get_pdfs` to attach documents: on PAID status, fetches the amalgamation application PDF and requests a receipt PDF from the payment service; on COMPLETED status, fetches the certificate of amalgamation PDF and notice of articles PDF. Each PDF is base64-encoded and appended with sequential attachment order. Calls `get_recipients` to retrieve email recipients from filing data; returns empty dict if none found. Sets email subject: "business legalName - Amalgamation" for PAID, "business legalName - Confirmation of Amalgamation" for COMPLETED. Returns dict with recipients, requestBy: 'BCRegistries@gov.bc.ca', and content object containing subject, HTML body, and PDF attachments.

Receipt PDF retrieval on status 201: if payment service returns non-201, logs error and skips receipt attachment—no retry or exception raised. No duplicate guard on recipients or attachments.","defines":["process"],"uses":[{"name":"get_filing_info","direction":"sends","what":"Calls with filing ID; receives filing record, business dict, legislative timezone filing date, and legislative timezone effective date."},{"name":"Filing.Status.PAID","direction":"reads","what":"Compares against status value to branch PAID vs COMPLETED document attachment logic."},{"name":"Filing.Status.COMPLETED","direction":"reads","what":"Compares against status value to branch document attachment logic."},{"name":"Amalgamation.AmalgamationTypes","direction":"reads","what":"Reads regular, vertical, and horizontal enum names to map to application names and to identify business role lookup."},{"name":"AmalgamatingBusiness.Role","direction":"reads","what":"Reads holding and primary role names to filter amalgamating businesses."},{"name":"Business.find_by_identifier","direction":"sends","what":"Calls with business identifier to retrieve primary or holding business record for legal name."},{"name":"Business.BUSINESSES","direction":"reads","what":"Reads business type config dict to look up numbered description by legal type."},{"name":"get_filing_document","direction":"sends","what":"Calls with business identifier, filing ID, document type (amalgamationApplication, certificateOfAmalgamation, noticeOfArticles), and token; receives base64-encoded PDF or falsy."},{"name":"PAY_API_URL","direction":"reads","what":"Config key; used to build payment service receipt endpoint URL."},{"name":"pay service /receipts endpoint","direction":"sends","what":"POSTs with Authorization: Bearer token header and JSON payload (corpName, filingDateTime, effectiveDateTime, filingIdentifier, businessNumber); expects 201 status. Returns receipt PDF in response.content on success."},{"name":"get_entity_dashboard_url","direction":"sends","what":"Calls with business identifier and token; receives dashboard URL for template rendering."},{"name":"substitute_template_parts","direction":"sends","what":"Calls with HTML template string; receives filled template with substitutions applied."},{"name":"Template","direction":"sends","what":"Jinja2 Template class instantiated with filled HTML and autoescape=True; renders with business, filing data, status, header, dates, URLs, and naming vars."},{"name":"get_recipients","direction":"sends","what":"Calls with status, filing JSON, token, and filing type; receives email recipient list or empty."},{"name":"TEMPLATE_PATH","direction":"reads","what":"Config key; used to read HTML email template file AMALGA-{status}.html from filesystem."},{"name":"logger.debug, logger.error","direction":"sends","what":"Logs filing notification and receipt fetch failures."}]}

