38538.text:
{"condensed":"Builds email notifications for business number assignment and moves in the entity-emailer system.

`process()` takes an email message with identifier and option, finds the business and one filing of type amalgamationApplication, continuationIn, incorporationApplication, or registration, loads and fills the BC-BN.html template with business json and entity description, gets recipients from filing.filing_json and filing_type, returns dict with recipients, requestBy: 'BCRegistries@gov.bc.ca', subject line with business legal_name, HTML body, and empty attachments. This chunk shows no check on caller.

`process_bn_move()` takes email message with identifier and nested data (oldBn, newBn) plus auth token, loads and fills BN-MOVE.html template with business json, entity description, oldBn and newBn. Builds recipients: adds business email from auth token lookup; if legal_type is SOLE_PROP, adds email from all non-ceased PROPRIETOR party_roles; if PARTNERSHIP, adds email from all non-ceased PARTNER party_roles. Deduplicates and joins recipients as comma-separated string. Returns dict with recipients string, requestBy: 'BCRegistries@gov.bc.ca', subject with "Business Number Changed", HTML body, empty attachments. This chunk shows no check on caller.","defines":["process","process_bn_move"],"uses":[{"name":"logger","direction":"sends","what":"Debug log with email message summary, from entity_queue_common.service_utils"},{"name":"current_app.config.get","direction":"reads","what":"TEMPLATE_PATH key to retrieve template directory path"},{"name":"Path.read_text","direction":"reads","what":"Reads BC-BN.html or BN-MOVE.html template file content from TEMPLATE_PATH"},{"name":"substitute_template_parts","direction":"sends","what":"Called to fill template placeholders, from entity_emailer.email_processors"},{"name":"Business.find_by_identifier","direction":"reads","what":"Queries legal_api.models.Business table by identifier; returns business or None"},{"name":"Filing.get_filings_by_types","direction":"reads","what":"Queries legal_api.models.Filing by business.id and filing type list; returns filing list"},{"name":"CorpType.find_by_id","direction":"reads","what":"Queries legal_api.models.CorpType by business.legal_type; returns corp_type or None"},{"name":"get_recipients","direction":"sends","what":"Called with email_msg option, filing.filing_json, filing.filing_type; returns recipient list from entity_emailer.email_processors"},{"name":"get_recipient_from_auth","direction":"sends","what":"Called with business.identifier and auth token; returns business email from entity_emailer.email_processors"},{"name":"PartyRole.get_parties_by_role","direction":"reads","what":"Queries legal_api.models.PartyRole by business.id and role value; returns party_role list"},{"name":"Business.LegalTypes.SOLE_PROP.value","direction":"reads","what":"Legal type constant from legal_api.models.Business enum"},{"name":"Business.LegalTypes.PARTNERSHIP.value","direction":"reads","what":"Legal type constant from legal_api.models.Business enum"},{"name":"PartyRole.RoleTypes.PROPRIETOR.value","direction":"reads","what":"Role type constant from legal_api.models.PartyRole enum"},{"name":"PartyRole.RoleTypes.PARTNER.value","direction":"reads","what":"Role type constant from legal_api.models.PartyRole enum"}]}

38541.text:
{"condensed":"Builds an email notification for a Continuation In filing in the Business Registry, with receipt or certificate attachments depending on filing status.

Entry point: `process(email_info, token)` — called by the email processor to build the notification; this chunk shows no check. Receives email_info dict with filing_id, type, option (status); retrieves filing details via `get_filing_info()`, extracts business and filing data from the filing JSON. For PAID status, substitutes the nameRequest business from filing_data. Fetches the foreign jurisdiction name by looking up country and region codes in pycountry. Loads template `CONT-IN-{status}.html` from TEMPLATE_PATH config, substitutes template parts, renders with Jinja2 passing business, filing_data, dates, entity_dashboard_url, filing_name, numbered_description, foreign_jurisdiction, and latest_review_comment (fetched from ReviewResult, with newlines encoded). Calls `_get_pdfs()` to gather attachments: for PAID, fetches 'continuationIn' PDF and posts to PAY_API_URL with payment_token to generate receipt (logs error if status != 201, does not retry); for RESUBMITTED, fetches 'continuationIn' PDF; for COMPLETED, fetches 'certificateOfContinuation' and 'noticeOfArticles' PDFs. Calls `get_recipients()` to get email recipients; returns empty dict if none. Assigns subject based on status. Returns dict with recipients, requestBy 'BCRegistries@gov.bc.ca', and content (subject, HTML body, PDF attachments).

GOTCHA: Receipt generation to PAY_API_URL is not retried on failure, only logged. GOTCHA: No check that filing exists or is valid before processing. GOTCHA: ReviewResult comment encoding and HTML decoding of newlines could cause display issues if comment contains literal '\n' strings.","defines":["process"],"uses":[{"name":"get_filing_info","direction":"sends","what":"Called with email_info['filingId'] to retrieve filing, business, and timezone-adjusted filing/effective dates."},{"name":"get_filing_document","direction":"sends","what":"Called with business identifier, filing id, document type ('continuationIn', 'certificateOfContinuation', 'noticeOfArticles'), and token; returns base64-encoded PDF or None."},{"name":"PAY_API_URL","direction":"sends","what":"Config key for payment API endpoint; posts to {PAY_API_URL}/{payment_token}/receipts with Bearer token auth, sending corpName, filingDateTime, effectiveDateTime, filingIdentifier, businessNumber; expects 201 status; logs error on failure, does not retry."},{"name":"pycountry.countries","direction":"reads","what":"Looks up country by alpha_2 code from filing_data['foreignJurisdiction']['country']."},{"name":"pycountry.subdivisions","direction":"reads","what":"Looks up region by code '{country_code}-{region_code}' from filing_data['foreignJurisdiction']['region'] if present and not 'FEDERAL'."},{"name":"TEMPLATE_PATH","direction":"reads","what":"Config key for template directory; loads file 'CONT-IN-{status}.html'."},{"name":"substitute_template_parts","direction":"sends","what":"Called with template text to substitute template parts."},{"name":"Template","direction":"sends","what":"Jinja2 Template initialized with filled template and autoescape=True; renders with business, filing_data, filing_status, header, dates, entity_dashboard_url, filing_name, filing_type, numbered_description, foreign_jurisdiction, latest_review_comment."},{"name":"get_entity_dashboard_url","direction":"sends","what":"Called with business identifier and token to get dashboard URL for the entity."},{"name":"get_recipients","direction":"sends","what":"Called with status, filing.filing_json, token, filing_type to retrieve email recipients; returns empty/falsy if none found."},{"name":"ReviewResult.get_last_review_result","direction":"reads","what":"Retrieves last review result for filing.id to extract comments; may be None."},{"name":"Business.BUSINESSES","direction":"reads","what":"Looks up legal_type to get numbered business description."},{"name":"Filing.Status","direction":"reads","what":"Enum with values PAID, COMPLETED, APPROVED, REJECTED, CHANGE_REQUESTED used for status comparison."},{"name":"logger","direction":"sends","what":"Logs debug message with filing_notification; logs error if receipt PDF generation fails."}]}

38545.text:
{"condensed":"Builds the email notification for a Business Registry dissolution filing. Entry point is `process(email_info, token)`, callable by a dissolution notification handler with no check shown. Inputs: email_info dict with keys `type`, `option`, `filingId`; token string. Outputs: dict with `recipients` (comma-separated emails), `requestBy` (BCRegistries@gov.bc.ca), `content` (subject, body HTML, attachments list).

Flow: retrieves filing, business, and filing dates via `get_filing_info(filingId)`; reads template from config path `TEMPLATE_PATH/DIS-{status}.html`; substitutes template parts and renders Jinja template with business, filing, header, dates, dashboard URL, filing name, and type; calls `_get_pdfs(status, token, business, filing, dates)` for attachments; builds recipients list by calling `get_recipient_from_auth(identifier, token)` and conditionally `get_user_email_from_auth(submitter.username, token)`. Decisions: if status is PAID and legal_type in [SP, GP], subject is "Confirmation of Filing from the Business Registry", else "Voluntary dissolution"; if status is COMPLETED and legal_type in [SP, GP], subject is "Dissolution Documents from the Business Registry", else "Confirmation of Dissolution from the Business Registry"; fallback subject is "Notification from the BC Business Registry". If legal_type is SP or GP, adds all party and party_role emails; else adds only Custodian role emails. Deduplicates and filters null recipients.

GOTCHA: no check shown for caller authorization; no check shown for token validity; subject assignment uses uninitialized `subject` variable with fallback only after conditionals.","defines":["process"],"uses":[{"name":"get_filing_info","direction":"sends","what":"calls with filingId from email_info, receives filing object with json, filing_type, submitter_roles, filing_submitter, business_id; filing_json with nested filing data; filing dates"},{"name":"substitute_template_parts","direction":"sends","what":"calls with template string, returns modified template"},{"name":"Template","direction":"sends","what":"Jinja2 Template class, instantiated with filled_template and autoescape=True, renders with business, filing, header, dates, URLs, email_header, filing_type"},{"name":"current_app.config","direction":"reads","what":"reads TEMPLATE_PATH for template directory and DASHBOARD_URL for entity dashboard base URL"},{"name":"_get_pdfs","direction":"sends","what":"calls with status, token, business, filing, two date objects; returns list of PDF attachment objects"},{"name":"get_recipient_from_auth","direction":"sends","what":"calls with identifier and token; returns primary recipient email from auth service"},{"name":"UserRoles.staff","direction":"reads","what":"constant checked against filing.submitter_roles to determine if staff filed the dissolution"},{"name":"Filing.Status.PAID","direction":"reads","what":"constant for paid filing status value"},{"name":"Filing.Status.COMPLETED","direction":"reads","what":"constant for completed filing status value"},{"name":"get_user_email_from_auth","direction":"sends","what":"calls with submitter username and token; returns user email from auth service"},{"name":"Business.find_by_internal_id","direction":"sends","what":"calls with filing.business_id; returns business object with party_roles collection"}]}

39286.text:
{"condensed":"Configuration module for a Flask authentication service that centralizes all environment variables and application settings. Loads environment values from a .env file or system variables, or provides defaults. Exports configuration objects (ProdConfig, TestConfig, DevConfig) and a factory function get_named_config() to return the appropriate config class based on environment name.

Reads from environment (or .env file): DATABASE_USERNAME, DATABASE_PASSWORD, DATABASE_NAME, DATABASE_HOST, DATABASE_PORT, DATABASE_UNIX_SOCKET; JWT_OIDC_WELL_KNOWN_CONFIG, JWT_OIDC_ALGORITHMS, JWT_OIDC_JWKS_URI, JWT_OIDC_ISSUER, JWT_OIDC_AUDIENCE, JWT_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET, JWT_OIDC_CACHING_ENABLED, JWT_OIDC_JWKS_CACHE_TIMEOUT (default 300); KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL, KEYCLOAK_REALMNAME, SBC_AUTH_ADMIN_CLIENT_ID, SBC_AUTH_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET; ACCESS_TOKEN_LIFESPAN (default 300); CACHE_MEMCACHED_SERVERS, CACHE_REDIS_HOST, CACHE_REDIS_PORT; ENTITY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_CLIENT_ID, ENTITY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_CLIENT_SECRET; KEYCLOAK_BCROS_* settings; API endpoints (BCOL_API_URL, LEGAL_API_URL, NAMEX_API_URL, NOTIFY_API_URL, PAY_API_SANDBOX_URL, PAY_API_URL); ACCOUNT_MAILER_TOPIC (default 'account-mailer-dev'), AUTH_EVENT_TOPIC (default 'auth-event-dev'), GCP_AUTH_KEY; Minio credentials and bucket; email and token configuration; Sentry settings; WEB_APP_URL, BCEID routes; MAX_NUMBER_OF_ORGS (default 3); BCOL_ACCOUNT_LINK_CHECK (default 'True'), DIRECT_PAY_ENABLED (default 'False'), DISABLE_ACTIVITY_LOGS (default 'False'); API Gateway settings; NR_SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPES (default 'BC'); AUTH_WEB_SANDBOX_HOST (default 'localhost'). Catches ValueError and bare exceptions when parsing int() for JWT_OIDC_JWKS_CACHE_TIMEOUT, CACHE_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT, MAX_NUMBER_OF_ORGS and silently falls back to defaults. get_named_config(config_name) raises KeyError if config_name is unknown. DevConfig sets TESTING=False, DEBUG=True, optionally disables Jaeger tracing logger.

GOTCHA: bare-except clauses swallow all exceptions silently with no logging. GOTCHA: SECRET_KEY hardcoded to 'a secret' in base class. GOTCHA: no validation that required keys (DATABASE_*, JWT_OIDC_*, KEYCLOAK_*) are actually set before use.","defines":["_Config","DevConfig","get_named_config","CONFIGURATION","PROJECT_ROOT","SECRET_KEY","AUTH_LD_SDK_KEY","TESTING","DEBUG","ALEMBIC_INI","SKIPPED_MIGRATIONS","DB_USER","DB_PASSWORD","DB_NAME","DB_HOST","DB_PORT","DB_UNIX_SOCKET","SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI","SQLALCHEMY_ECHO","SQLALCHEMY_TRACK_MODIFICATIONS","JWT_OIDC_WELL_KNOWN_CONFIG","JWT_OIDC_ALGORITHMS","JWT_OIDC_JWKS_URI","JWT_OIDC_ISSUER","JWT_OIDC_AUDIENCE","JWT_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET","JWT_OIDC_CACHING_ENABLED","JWT_OIDC_JWKS_CACHE_TIMEOUT","KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL","KEYCLOAK_REALMNAME","KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_USERNAME","KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_SECRET","CACHE_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT","CACHE_MEMCACHED_SERVERS","CACHE_REDIS_HOST","CACHE_REDIS_PORT","KEYCLOAK_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_ID","KEYCLOAK_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_SECRET","ENTITY_SVC_CLIENT_ID","ENTITY_SVC_CLIENT_SECRET","KEYCLOAK_BCROS_BASE_URL","KEYCLOAK_BCROS_REALMNAME","KEYCLOAK_BCROS_ADMIN_CLIENTID","KEYCLOAK_BCROS_ADMIN_SECRET","BCOL_API_URL","LEGAL_API_URL","NAMEX_API_URL","NOTIFY_API_URL","PAY_API_SANDBOX_URL","PAY_API_URL","LEGAL_API_VERSION","LEGAL_API_VERSION_2","LEAR_AFFILIATION_DETAILS_URL","NAMEX_AFFILIATION_DETAILS_URL","ACCOUNT_MAILER_TOPIC","AUTH_EVENT_TOPIC","GCP_AUTH_KEY","MINIO_ENDPOINT","MINIO_ACCESS_KEY","MINIO_ACCESS_SECRET","MINIO_BUCKET_ACCOUNTS","MINIO_SECURE","MAIL_FROM_ID","EMAIL_SECURITY_PASSWORD_SALT","EMAIL_TOKEN_SECRET_KEY","TOKEN_EXPIRY_PERIOD","AFFILIATION_TOKEN_EXPIRY_PERIOD_MINS","STAFF_ADMIN_EMAIL","SENTRY_ENABLE","SENTRY_DSN","REGISTRIES_LOGO_IMAGE_NAME","WEB_APP_URL","BCEID_SIGNIN_ROUTE","BCEID_ACCOUNT_SETUP_ROUTE","BCEID_ADMIN_SETUP_ROUTE","MAX_NUMBER_OF_ORGS","BCOL_ACCOUNT_LINK_CHECK","DIRECT_PAY_ENABLED","DISABLE_ACTIVITY_LOGS","API_GW_CONSUMERS_API_URL","API_GW_KEY","API_GW_CONSUMERS_SANDBOX_API_URL","API_GW_NON_PROD_KEY","API_GW_EMAIL_SUFFIX","API_GW_KC_CLIENT_ID_PATTERN","NR_SUPPORTED_REQUEST_TYPES","AUTH_WEB_SANDBOX_HOST"],"uses":[{"name":"dotenv.load_dotenv","direction":"sends","what":"Loads environment variables from .env file found by find_dotenv()."},{"name":"os.getenv","direction":"reads","what":"Reads environment variables; returns None or empty string if not set."},{"name":"Flask config","direction":"sends","what":"All modules load their configuration from Flask config object (of type _Config, DevConfig, TestConfig, or ProdConfig) rather than reading environment directly."},{"name":"logging.getLogger","direction":"sends","what":"DevConfig disables Jaeger tracing logger when DISABLE_JAEGER_TRACING is true."},{"name":"PostgreSQL","direction":"reads","what":"SQLALCHEMY_DATABASE_URI connects via psycopg2 to PostgreSQL; uses DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD, DB_NAME, DB_HOST, DB_PORT or DB_UNIX_SOCKET."},{"name":"Keycloak","direction":"reads","what":"Credentials for service account (SBC_AUTH_ADMIN_CLIENT_ID, SBC_AUTH_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET) and upstream Keycloak settings (KEYCLOAK_BCROS_*)."},{"name":"BCOL API","direction":"reads","what":"Endpoint URL in BCOL_API_URL."},{"name":"Legal API","direction":"reads","what":"Endpoint URL and versions in LEGAL_API_URL, LEGAL_API_VERSION, LEGAL_API_VERSION_2."},{"name":"Namex API","direction":"reads","what":"Endpoint URL in NAMEX_API_URL."},{"name":"Notify API","direction":"reads","what":"Endpoint URL in NOTIFY_API_URL."},{"name":"Pay API","direction":"reads","what":"Endpoint URLs in PAY_API_SANDBOX_URL and PAY_API_URL."},{"name":"GCP Pub/Sub","direction":"sends","what":"Topics ACCOUNT_MAILER_TOPIC (default 'account-mailer-dev') and AUTH_EVENT_TOPIC (default 'auth-event-dev') authenticated with GCP_AUTH_KEY."},{"name":"Minio","direction":"reads","what":"Object storage credentials in MINIO_ENDPOINT, MINIO_ACCESS_KEY, MINIO_ACCESS_SECRET; bucket MINIO_BUCKET_ACCOUNTS (default 'accounts')."},{"name":"Sentry","direction":"reads","what":"Error tracking enabled via SENTRY_ENABLE and SENTRY_DSN."},{"name":"API Gateway","direction":"reads","what":"Consumer API URLs (API_GW_CONSUMERS_API_URL, API_GW_CONSUMERS_SANDBOX_API_URL) and credentials (API_GW_KEY, API_GW_NON_PROD_KEY)."},{"name":"Alembic","direction":"reads","what":"Migration config at migrations/alembic.ini; skips migrations in SKIPPED_MIGRATIONS list."}]}

39301.text:
{"condensed":"Base model superclass for database models with audit tracking.

Provides audit columns (created, modified, created_by_id, modified_by_id) that track creation and modification timestamps and users via relationships to a User model; created_by_id and modified_by_id default to the current user via _get_current_user. Entry points are public methods callable by any code. update_from_dict accepts a dict and updates model fields, skipping readonly fields (id, created, modified, created_by_id, modified_by_id), private fields starting with _, and relationship fields; returns a dict of changes as {key: {old: val, new: val}} and accepts optional _exclude list. find_by_id retrieves a model by integer id. flush adds to session, flushes, and calls create_activity. save adds, flushes, calls create_activity, and commits. delete removes, flushes, calls create_activity with is_delete=True, and commits. commit, rollback, reset, and add_to_session are passthrough session operations. create_activity creates activity records for VersionedModel instances when DISABLE_ACTIVITY_LOGS is not set, with verb 'create' or 'update' (if modified_by is not None) or 'delete', capturing preferred_username from g.jwt_oidc_token_info and remote address. _get_current_user looks up current user by JWT token and returns user.id or None; swallows all exceptions. BaseCodeModel adds code (String 15, primary key), description (String 100), and default (Boolean, False) columns; its save method commits. VersionedModel marks models as versioned with empty exclude list.

GOTCHA: _get_current_user catches all exceptions and silently returns None. GOTCHA: create_activity checks isinstance(obj, VersionedModel) but is called from methods on BaseModel itself with a BaseModel instance, meaning activity is never actually created for non-VersionedModel subclasses. GOTCHA: update_from_dict skips private fields but this chunk shows no validation that excluded fields were intended to be excluded.","defines":["BaseModel","BaseCodeModel","VersionedModel","created_by_id","modified_by_id","created_by","modified_by","created","modified","find_by_id","update_from_dict","commit","flush","add_to_session","save","delete","rollback","reset","create_activity","code","description","default","__versioned__"],"uses":[{"name":"db","direction":"reads","what":"SQLAlchemy session and Model base class; db.session used for add, flush, commit, delete, rollback operations"},{"name":"current_app.config","direction":"reads","what":"DISABLE_ACTIVITY_LOGS flag to conditionally suppress activity logging"},{"name":"g","direction":"reads","what":"Flask g context object, checked for jwt_oidc_token_info containing preferred_username"},{"name":"activity_plugin.activity_cls","direction":"sends","what":"Creates and adds activity record to session with verb, object, and data dict including user_name and remote_addr; sent only for VersionedModel instances when DISABLE_ACTIVITY_LOGS is not set"},{"name":"fetch_remote_addr","direction":"sends","what":"Fetches remote client IP address from sqlalchemy_continuum.plugins.flask"},{"name":"User.find_by_jwt_token","direction":"sends","what":"Looks up User model by current JWT token to populate created_by and modified_by; called internally to get current user ID, returns None if not found or exception occurs"}]}

39362.text:
{"condensed":"Flask REST API for organization (org) management, including search, creation, retrieval, update and deletion. Requires JWT authentication with specific roles.

Entry points: (1) GET /orgs?... calls search_organizations, requires one of SYSTEM, STAFF_VIEW_ACCOUNTS, PUBLIC_USER roles; extracts name, branchName, affiliation, status, accessType, bcolAccountId, id, decisionMadeBy, orgType, page, limit from query; calls OrgService.find_by_org_name if validateName==TRUE, else OrgService.search_orgs; if caller is PUBLIC_USER without STAFF, SYSTEM or ACCOUNT_IDENTITY roles, returns empty response dict with 204 status when no results; catches BusinessException and returns code and message. (2) GET /orgs/simple?... calls search_simple_orgs, requires MANAGE_EFT or SYSTEM role (enforced by @validate_roles and @_jwt.has_one_of_roles); extracts id, page, limit, name, branchName, searchText, statuses (defaulting to ACTIVE), excludeStatuses; calls SimpleOrgService.search. (3) POST /orgs calls post_organization, requires PUBLIC_USER, STAFF_CREATE_ACCOUNTS or SYSTEM (not ANONYMOUS_USER); validates JSON against 'org' schema; calls UserService.find_by_jwt_token, returns 401 if null; calls OrgService.create_org with request_json and user.identifier. (4) GET /orgs/<org_id> calls get_organization, requires one of SYSTEM, STAFF_VIEW_ACCOUNTS, PUBLIC_USER; calls OrgService.find_by_org_id with ALL_ALLOWED_ROLES; returns 404 if not found. (5) PUT /orgs/<org_id> calls put_organization, requires SYSTEM, PUBLIC_USER, GOV_ACCOUNT_USER or STAFF_MANAGE_ACCOUNTS; validates JSON against 'org' schema; calls OrgService.find_by_org_id with CLIENT_ADMIN_ROLES and STAFF; if org has accessType==ANONYMOUS and caller lacks STAFF_CREATE_ACCOUNTS role, returns 401; calls org.update_org. (6) DELETE /orgs/<org_id> calls delete_organization, requires SYSTEM, STAFF_CREATE_ACCOUNTS or PUBLIC_USER; calls OrgService.delete_org, returns 204 on success. All routes decorated with @cross_origin and @TRACER.trace(). All BusinessExceptions caught and returned as {code, message} with exception.status_code.

GOTCHA: GET /orgs?validateName=TRUE bypasses OrgSearch pagination and returns only find_by_org_name result, differing from default search behaviour. GOTCHA: PUT /orgs/<org_id> checks accessType==ANONYMOUS and STAFF_CREATE_ACCOUNTS role but only after finding org with CLIENT_ADMIN_ROLES and STAFF filter; this allows non-matching roles to attempt update. GOTCHA: No check shown in post_organization that user actually has the role claimed by decorator, only that user was found via JWT.","defines":["GET /orgs","GET /orgs/simple","POST /orgs","GET /orgs/{org_id}","PUT /orgs/{org_id}","DELETE /orgs/{org_id}"],"uses":[{"name":"OrgService.find_by_org_name","direction":"sends","what":"Called with org_name and branch_name; returns org matching name and branch"},{"name":"OrgService.search_orgs","direction":"sends","what":"Called with OrgSearch object and env; returns paginated org search results matching filters"},{"name":"Role.STAFF.value, Role.SYSTEM.value, Role.ACCOUNT_IDENTITY","direction":"reads","what":"Role constants compared against user's realm_access roles to determine if PUBLIC_USER may see org results"},{"name":"SimpleOrgService.search","direction":"sends","what":"Called with SimpleOrgSearch; returns simplified org list filtered by id, name, branch_name, searchText, statuses, page, limit"},{"name":"UserService.find_by_jwt_token","direction":"sends","what":"Called with no args; returns user object or None; required before org creation"},{"name":"OrgService.create_org","direction":"sends","what":"Called with request_json and user.identifier; creates and returns new org or updates existing"},{"name":"OrgService.find_by_org_id","direction":"sends","what":"Called with org_id and allowed_roles; returns org matching id or None; used in GET, PUT, DELETE"},{"name":"org.update_org","direction":"sends","what":"Called with org_info dict; updates org attributes and returns updated org"},{"name":"OrgService.delete_org","direction":"sends","what":"Called with org_id; inactivates org if no active members or affiliations"},{"name":"schema_utils.validate","direction":"sends","what":"Called with request JSON and schema name 'org'; returns (valid_format, errors) tuple"},{"name":"g.jwt_oidc_token_info","direction":"reads","what":"Reads JWT token info from Flask g context; contains realm_access.roles and identifies caller"},{"name":"@_jwt.has_one_of_roles","direction":"receives","what":"Decorator enforcing caller has one of specified roles; raises if check fails"},{"name":"@validate_roles","direction":"receives","what":"Decorator validating allowed_roles and not_allowed_roles against caller's roles"},{"name":"BusinessException","direction":"receives","what":"Caught on all endpoints; contains code, message, status_code to return to caller"}]}

39561.text:
{"condensed":"Retrieves and searches organizations, refines access controls, validates BCOL account links, changes org status, and approves or rejects org applications with email notifications.

Entry points: `get_orgs(user_id, valid_statuses)` returns orgs for a user via `MembershipModel.find_orgs_for_user()`. `search_orgs(search, environment)` searches orgs; checks if caller has `Role.STAFF_CREATE_ACCOUNTS` or `Role.STAFF_MANAGE_ACCOUNTS` to view `OrgStatus.PENDING_ACTIVATION` orgs, raises `BusinessException(Error.INVALID_USER_CREDENTIALS)` if not staff and requesting pending activation, otherwise calls `OrgModel.search_pending_activation_orgs()` or `OrgModel.search_org()`, returns dict with `orgs` (array of org as_dict plus first contact and optionally first invitation), `page`, `limit`, `total`. `search_orgs_by_affiliation(business_identifier, environment, excluded_org_types)` calls `OrgModel.search_orgs_by_business_identifier()`, returns dict with `orgs` and `total`. `refine_access_type(access_types)` decorated with `@user_context`, strips `AccessType.ANONYMOUS` from access_types unless caller has staff roles, returns tuple (access_types, is_staff_admin). `bcol_account_link_check(bcol_account_id, org_id)` when `BCOL_ACCOUNT_LINK_CHECK` config is true, calls `OrgModel.find_by_bcol_id()`, returns True if a different org already claims the bcol_account_id. `change_org_status(status_code, suspension_reason_code)` gets current user via `UserModel.find_by_jwt_token()`, updates org status_code, decision_made_by, and if suspended sets suspended_on to today, suspension_reason_code, calls `org_model.save()`, publishes activity via `ActivityLogPublisher.publish_activity()` with activity name and suspension_reason_description (or empty string if code not in SuspensionReasonCode enum), returns Org. `approve_or_reject(org_id, is_approved, origin_url, task_action)` gets org via `OrgModel.find_by_org_id()`, gets current user via `UserModel.find_by_jwt_token()`, if task_action equals `TaskAction.AFFIDAVIT_REVIEW.value` calls `AffidavitService.approve_or_reject()`, sets org status to ACTIVE or REJECTED, decision_made_by, decision_made_on to now, calls `org.save()`, gets admin emails via `UserService.get_admin_emails_for_org()`, sends email via `Org.send_approved_rejected_notification()` or `Org.send_approved_rejected_govm_govn_notification()` depending on access_type, logs error if no admin emails, returns Org. `send_staff_review_account_reminder(relationship_id, task_relationship_type)` gets current user via `UserModel.find_by_jwt_token()`, reads `STAFF_ADMIN_EMAIL` config, gets task via `TaskModel.find_by_task_relationship_id()`, builds review URL from origin_url and task.id, publishes to mailer queue `QueueMessageTypes.STAFF_REVIEW_ACCOUNT.value` with emailAddresses, contextUrl, userFirstName, userLastName, on exception logs error and raises `BusinessException(Error.FAILED_NOTIFICATION)`. `send_approved_rejected_notification(receipt_admin_emails, org_name, org_id, org_status, origin_url)` selects notification type based on org_status (ACTIVE or REJECTED), publishes to mailer queue with accountId, emailAddresses, contextUrl, orgName, on exception logs error and raises `BusinessException(Error.FAILED_NOTIFICATION)`.

GOTCHA: `change_org_status()` shows no permission check; comment says "only staff can do it now" but code lacks enforcement. GOTCHA: `approve_or_reject()` comment says "TODO Publish to activity stream" but only publishes for suspension. GOTCHA: Both send_*_notification methods swallow exception, log it, and re-raise as `BusinessException`; if mailer queue fails, org status persists as already saved.","defines":["get_orgs","search_orgs","search_orgs_by_affiliation","refine_access_type","bcol_account_link_check","change_org_status","approve_or_reject","send_staff_review_account_reminder","send_approved_rejected_notification"],"uses":[{"name":"MembershipModel.find_orgs_for_user","direction":"sends","what":"Finds orgs associated with user_id and valid_statuses list."},{"name":"OrgModel.search_pending_activation_orgs","direction":"sends","what":"Searches orgs with PENDING_ACTIVATION status by name; caller must have Role.STAFF_CREATE_ACCOUNTS or Role.STAFF_MANAGE_ACCOUNTS or BusinessException raised."},{"name":"OrgModel.search_org","direction":"sends","what":"Searches orgs by OrgSearch criteria and environment."},{"name":"OrgModel.find_by_bcol_id","direction":"sends","what":"Finds org by bcol_account_id when BCOL_ACCOUNT_LINK_CHECK config enabled."},{"name":"OrgModel.find_by_org_id","direction":"sends","what":"Finds org by org_id."},{"name":"OrgModel.search_orgs_by_business_identifier","direction":"sends","what":"Searches orgs by business_identifier, environment, and excluded_org_types list."},{"name":"UserModel.find_by_jwt_token","direction":"sends","what":"Gets current authenticated user from JWT token in request."},{"name":"ActivityLogPublisher.publish_activity","direction":"sends","what":"Publishes activity event with org_id, ActivityAction.ACCOUNT_SUSPENSION, org name and suspension_reason_description."},{"name":"AffidavitService.approve_or_reject","direction":"sends","what":"Approves or rejects affidavit for org when task_action is TaskAction.AFFIDAVIT_REVIEW."},{"name":"UserService.get_admin_emails_for_org","direction":"sends","what":"Gets comma-separated admin email string for org_id."},{"name":"TaskModel.find_by_task_relationship_id","direction":"sends","what":"Finds task by task_relationship_type and relationship_id."},{"name":"publish_to_mailer","direction":"sends","what":"Publishes message to mailer queue with notification type and data dict containing emailAddresses, contextUrl, userFirstName, userLastName (or accountId, emailAddresses, contextUrl, orgName for approval notification)."},{"name":"BCOL_ACCOUNT_LINK_CHECK","direction":"reads","what":"Config boolean flag enabling BCOL account link validation."},{"name":"STAFF_ADMIN_EMAIL","direction":"reads","what":"Config string with staff admin email recipient."},{"name":"QueueMessageTypes.STAFF_REVIEW_ACCOUNT","direction":"sends","what":"Queue message type for staff review account reminder notification."},{"name":"QueueMessageTypes.NON_BCSC_ORG_APPROVED_NOTIFICATION","direction":"sends","what":"Queue message type for org approved notification."},{"name":"QueueMessageTypes.NON_BCSC_ORG_REJECTED_NOTIFICATION","direction":"sends","what":"Queue message type for org rejected notification."},{"name":"VALID_STATUSES","direction":"reads","what":"Default valid org statuses for get_orgs filter."},{"name":"AccessType.ANONYMOUS","direction":"reads","what":"Access type enum value filtered from search unless staff admin."},{"name":"AccessType.EXTRA_PROVINCIAL","direction":"reads","what":"Access type enum checked to route to standard approval notification."},{"name":"AccessType.REGULAR_BCEID","direction":"reads","what":"Access type enum checked to route to standard approval notification."},{"name":"AccessType.GOVM","direction":"reads","what":"Access type enum checked to route to GOVM/GOVN approval notification."},{"name":"AccessType.GOVN","direction":"reads","what":"Access type enum checked to route to GOVM/GOVN approval notification."},{"name":"OrgStatus.PENDING_ACTIVATION","direction":"reads","what":"Org status enum; only staff admin can search this status."},{"name":"OrgStatus.SUSPENDED","direction":"reads","what":"Org status enum for suspension status code."},{"name":"OrgStatus.ACTIVE","direction":"reads","what":"Org status enum for active status on approval."},{"name":"OrgStatus.REJECTED","direction":"reads","what":"Org status enum for rejected status on rejection."},{"name":"Role.STAFF_CREATE_ACCOUNTS","direction":"reads","what":"Role enum indicating staff admin permission."},{"name":"Role.STAFF_MANAGE_ACCOUNTS","direction":"reads","what":"Role enum indicating staff admin permission."},{"name":"SuspensionReasonCode","direction":"reads","what":"Enum of suspension reason codes; looked up by name to get description value."},{"name":"TaskAction.AFFIDAVIT_REVIEW","direction":"reads","what":"Task action enum value triggering affidavit approval service."},{"name":"TaskRelationshipType.ORG","direction":"reads","what":"Task relationship type enum for org-related tasks."},{"name":"Error.INVALID_USER_CREDENTIALS","direction":"reads","what":"Error code raised when non-staff searches pending activation orgs."},{"name":"Error.FAILED_NOTIFICATION","direction":"reads","what":"Error code raised when notification publish fails."},{"name":"Org","direction":"sends","what":"Wraps org model; as_dict() returns org dict, send_approved_rejected_notification and send_approved_rejected_govm_govn_notification are called as static methods."},{"name":"ContactSchema","direction":"reads","what":"Schema dumping first contact with 'links' excluded."},{"name":"InvitationSchema","direction":"reads","what":"Schema dumping first invitation with 'membership' excluded."},{"name":"user_context","direction":"receives","what":"Decorator providing user_context kwarg from JWT token."},{"name":"g.get","direction":"reads","what":"Flask g object reads 'origin_url' from request context."},{"name":"current_app","direction":"reads","what":"Flask app context for logger, config, and logging."},{"name":"datetime.today","direction":"reads","what":"Gets current date for suspended_on field."},{"name":"datetime.now","direction":"reads","what":"Gets current datetime for decision_made_on field."}]}

39603.text:
{"condensed":"Extends Flask-SQLAlchemy's BaseQuery class to provide conditional filtering helper for database queries in a Flask application.

The `filter_conditionally` method accepts a search_criteria value, a model_attribute to filter on, and an optional is_like boolean flag. It returns the query object unchanged if search_criteria is None. For datetime or date instances, it filters by the date component using SQL's DATE function. When is_like is true, it casts the attribute to String and applies case-insensitive pattern matching with ILIKE and wildcard delimiters, using SQLAlchemy functions to prevent SQL injection. Otherwise it performs exact equality matching. The method returns self to enable query chaining.

GOTCHA: The comment notes LIKE searches must use SQLAlchemy functions for bind variables to mitigate SQL injection, but the exact equality branch (the final filter call) does not explicitly call out what injection protections apply there.","defines":["CustomQuery","filter_conditionally"],"uses":[{"name":"BaseQuery","direction":"reads","what":"Flask-SQLAlchemy base query class that CustomQuery extends"},{"name":"func","direction":"reads","what":"SQLAlchemy functions used for DATE casting and ILIKE pattern matching"},{"name":"String","direction":"reads","what":"SQLAlchemy String type used for casting model attributes"},{"name":"datetime, date","direction":"reads","what":"Python standard types checked to determine filter logic"}]}

39613.text:
{"condensed":"Utility module providing helper functions for data transformation, URL encoding, email masking, and environment detection in a Flask application.

Exports six functions and one metaclass. `camelback2snake` and `snake2camelback` convert dictionary keys between camelCase and snake_case using the humps library. `digitify` extracts and returns digits from a string via regex substitution. `escape_wam_friendly_url` base64-encodes a parameter then URL-encodes it with no safe characters. `mask_email` returns an email with username and domain each masked to first two characters plus asterisks for the remainder, or the original email if input is falsy or lacks an @ separator. `extract_numbers` returns a string of only digit characters from input, or None if input is None. `get_request_environment` returns 'sandbox' if FLASK_ENV is production and AUTH_WEB_SANDBOX_HOST appears in the current request's host URL, otherwise None. `Singleton` is a metaclass implementing singleton pattern via a class-level _instances dict checked in __call__.

GOTCHA: mask_email silently returns the original email if it cannot split on exactly one @ character, rather than raising or logging a concern.","defines":["camelback2snake","snake2camelback","Singleton","digitify","escape_wam_friendly_url","mask_email","get_request_environment","extract_numbers"],"uses":[{"name":"decamelize","direction":"sends","what":"Function from humps.main called to convert dictionary keys from camelCase to snake_case."},{"name":"camelize","direction":"sends","what":"Function from humps.main called to convert dictionary keys from snake_case to camelCase."},{"name":"current_app","direction":"reads","what":"Flask current_app context accessed to read AUTH_WEB_SANDBOX_HOST config value."},{"name":"request","direction":"reads","what":"Flask request object accessed to read request.host_url for environment detection."},{"name":"AUTH_WEB_SANDBOX_HOST","direction":"reads","what":"Flask config key containing sandbox host string, read to determine if request is sandbox environment."}]}

40301.text:
{"condensed":"SignoutView is a Vue component that handles user logout by clearing application state and redirecting to a configured destination. When mounted, the component clears all Vuex store state via replaceState({}) and resets all application stores via resetAllStores(). It delegates the actual logout UI and process to the SbcSignout child component, passing it a redirect URL.

The redirect URL is determined by the redirectbackUrl computed property: if the redirectUrl prop is empty, it defaults to ConfigHelper.getRegistryHomeURL() with '/login' appended; otherwise it uses the provided prop value. GOTCHA: the TODO comment indicates incomplete logic—"need to fix for one URL"—suggesting redirect handling may not work correctly in some cases. The component shows no permission check.

Entry point: mounted lifecycle hook, called automatically by Vue when the component is instantiated. Callouts: ConfigHelper.getRegistryHomeURL() reads configuration; resetAllStores() clears all application stores; SbcSignout component handles logout delegation.","defines":["SignoutView"],"uses":[{"name":"ConfigHelper.getRegistryHomeURL","direction":"sends","what":"Reads registry home URL from configuration to construct default redirect URL for post-logout navigation."},{"name":"resetAllStores","direction":"sends","what":"Clears all application stores (Pinia or other store implementations) during logout."},{"name":"SbcSignout","direction":"sends","what":"Child component that performs the actual logout operation; receives redirectbackUrl prop to determine post-logout redirect destination."},{"name":"Vue","direction":"receives","what":"Component lifecycle: mounted hook is called automatically when component is instantiated."},{"name":"this.$store.replaceState","direction":"sends","what":"Vuex store method that clears all state by replacing it with empty object during logout."}]}

