42388.text:
{"condensed":"Service to manage electronic fund transfers via EFT payment method with PAYBC system code.

Entry points: `get_payment_method_code()` (public, no check shown) returns PaymentMethod.EFT.value; `get_payment_system_code()` (public, no check shown) returns PaymentSystem.PAYBC.value; `create_account(identifier, contact_info, payment_info)` (public, no check shown) creates CfsAccountModel with status PENDING and payment_method EFT; `create_invoice(payment_account, line_items, invoice)` (public, no check shown) calls `ensure_no_payment_blockers()` then does nothing (invoice references created by separate create_cfs_invoices job); `complete_post_invoice(invoice, invoice_reference)` (public, no check shown) calls `_release_payment()` with invoice; `get_default_invoice_status()` (public, no check shown) returns InvoiceStatus.APPROVED.value; `create_payment(payment_account, invoice, payment_date, paid_amount)` (public, no check shown) returns PaymentModel with method EFT, status COMPLETED, system PAYBC, invoice_number prefixed by config EFT_INVOICE_PREFIX, receipt_number set to invoice.id; `process_cfs_refund(invoice, payment_account, refund_partial)` (public, no check shown) - if invoice status is APPROVED and no active InvoiceReference and no EFTCreditInvoiceLinks exist, returns CANCELLED; if active completed consolidated InvoiceReference exists, raises BusinessException(Error.INVALID_CONSOLIDATED_REFUND); otherwise calls EFTRefundService.handle_invoice_refund(); `create_invoice_reference(invoice, invoice_number, reference_number)` (static, no check shown) finds or creates InvoiceReferenceModel, sets status ACTIVE; `create_receipt(invoice, payment)` (static, no check shown) returns ReceiptModel; `apply_payment_action(short_name_id, auth_account_id)` (static, checks auth_account_id not None and PaymentAccountModel.find_by_auth_account_id returns non-None, raises BusinessException(Error.EFT_PAYMENT_ACTION_ACCOUNT_ID_REQUIRED) if fails) calls EftService.process_owing_statements(); `cancel_payment_action(short_name_id, auth_account_id, invoice_id)` (static, checks auth_account_id not None and payment_account found, raises BusinessException(Error.EFT_PAYMENT_ACTION_ACCOUNT_ID_REQUIRED) if fails) - gets EFTCreditInvoiceLinks with status PENDING via `_get_shortname_invoice_links()`, for each calls EFTRefundService.return_eft_credit() to status CANCELLED, collects link_group_ids, deletes associated EFTHistoryModels, flushes to database.

GOTCHA: `process_cfs_refund()` return value is inconsistent - sometimes returns InvoiceStatus value string, sometimes returns what EFTRefundService.handle_invoice_refund() returns (type unclear); consolidated refund rejection message does not explain why consolidation blocks refunds.","defines":["get_payment_method_code","get_payment_system_code","create_account","create_invoice","complete_post_invoice","get_default_invoice_status","create_payment","process_cfs_refund","create_invoice_reference","create_receipt","apply_payment_action","cancel_payment_action"],"uses":[{"name":"PaymentMethod.EFT","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for EFT payment method code"},{"name":"PaymentSystem.PAYBC","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for PAYBC system code"},{"name":"CfsAccountModel","direction":"sends","what":"creates account instance with status and payment_method"},{"name":"CfsAccountStatus.PENDING","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for account status"},{"name":"current_app.logger","direction":"sends","what":"logs info and debug messages"},{"name":"current_app.config","direction":"reads","what":"reads EFT_INVOICE_PREFIX configuration key"},{"name":"PaymentModel","direction":"sends","what":"creates payment record with method, status, system, invoice number, amounts, account and date"},{"name":"PaymentStatus.COMPLETED","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for payment status"},{"name":"InvoiceStatus.APPROVED","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for invoice status"},{"name":"InvoiceStatus.CANCELLED","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for cancelled invoice status"},{"name":"ensure_no_payment_blockers","direction":"sends","what":"checks payment account for blockers"},{"name":"_release_payment","direction":"sends","what":"publishes message to queue with payment token"},{"name":"EFTCreditInvoiceLinkModel.find_by_invoice_id","direction":"sends","what":"retrieves credit invoice links for invoice"},{"name":"InvoiceReferenceModel.find_by_invoice_id_and_status","direction":"sends","what":"retrieves invoice reference by id and status"},{"name":"InvoiceReferenceStatus.ACTIVE","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for active reference status"},{"name":"InvoiceReferenceStatus.COMPLETED","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for completed reference status"},{"name":"BusinessException","direction":"sends","what":"raises exception with Error.INVALID_CONSOLIDATED_REFUND"},{"name":"Error.INVALID_CONSOLIDATED_REFUND","direction":"reads","what":"error constant for consolidated refund rejection"},{"name":"EFTRefundService.handle_invoice_refund","direction":"sends","what":"handles refund processing for invoice, payment account and credit invoice links"},{"name":"InvoiceReferenceModel.find_any_active_reference_by_invoice_number","direction":"sends","what":"finds active invoice reference by number"},{"name":"InvoiceReferenceModel","direction":"sends","what":"creates or updates invoice reference with id, number, status"},{"name":"ReceiptModel","direction":"sends","what":"creates receipt with date, amount, invoice id, number"},{"name":"PaymentAccountModel.find_by_auth_account_id","direction":"sends","what":"retrieves payment account by auth account id"},{"name":"Error.EFT_PAYMENT_ACTION_ACCOUNT_ID_REQUIRED","direction":"reads","what":"error constant for missing auth account id"},{"name":"EftService.process_owing_statements","direction":"sends","what":"processes outstanding payments for account"},{"name":"EftService._get_shortname_invoice_links","direction":"sends","what":"retrieves EFTCreditInvoiceLinks by short name, account, optional invoice id, and statuses"},{"name":"EFTCreditInvoiceStatus.PENDING","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for pending credit status"},{"name":"EFTRefundService.return_eft_credit","direction":"sends","what":"returns EFT credit with new status for a credit link"},{"name":"EFTCreditInvoiceStatus.CANCELLED","direction":"reads","what":"enum value for cancelled credit status"},{"name":"db.session","direction":"sends","what":"adds, deletes and flushes models to database"},{"name":"EFTHistoryModel.find_by_related_group_link_id","direction":"sends","what":"retrieves history model by link group id"}]}

42389.text:
{"condensed":"Reverses EFT payments applied to invoices on a statement, returning credits to a short name's EFT account and notifying account admins of the adjusted balance.

Entry point `reverse_payment_action(short_name_id, statement_id)` is a static method; this chunk shows no permission check. It requires a non-null `statement_id`, raising `BusinessException(Error.EFT_PAYMENT_ACTION_STATEMENT_ID_REQUIRED)` if absent. Fetches credit-invoice links for the short name and statement, validates them (no links in PENDING, PENDING_REFUND, or REFUNDED status; payment date must be within 60 days), then iterates each link. Skips invoices in REFUND_REQUESTED, REFUNDED, or CANCELLED status. For PAID invoices only, calls `EFTRefundService.return_eft_credit(link)` to reverse the credit, creates a new `EFTCreditInvoiceLinkModel` with status PENDING_REFUND, and accumulates reversed amounts. After iteration, creates an `EFTHistory` record via `EFTHistoryService.create_statement_reverse()` with the total reversed amount and current EFT credit balance. Sends email notification to payment account admins with reversed amount and recalculated outstanding balance. All database writes are flushed individually but within a single request (no explicit transaction control shown). Commented-out partner disbursement code suggests incomplete feature. Helper `get_pending_payment_count()` returns a subquery for PENDING link counts by payment account. Helper `_get_shortname_invoice_links()` queries links by short name, account, and status list, optionally filtered by invoice. Helper `_validate_reversal_credit_invoice_links()` enforces the validation rules above. Helper `_send_reversed_payment_notification()` decorated with `@user_context`, retrieves admin contacts via external `get_account_admin_users()` call and sends email via `send_email()`. Helper `get_statement_credit_invoice_links()` retrieves the most recent link per invoice for a statement and short name, excluding cancelled links.

GOTCHA: No duplicate guard prevents reversing the same statement twice. GOTCHA: Reversed credits are recorded (EFTHistory) after individual link processing completes; partial reversal (if an invoice fails mid-loop) leaves EFTHistory inconsistent with actual reversed links. GOTCHA: Email sending failures are not retried and do not block the reversal. GOTCHA: Partner disbursement logic is commented out and incomplete.","defines":["reverse_payment_action","get_pending_payment_count","_get_shortname_invoice_links","_send_reversed_payment_notification","_validate_reversal_credit_invoice_links","get_statement_credit_invoice_links"],"uses":[{"name":"BusinessException","direction":"sends","what":"Raised with specific error codes (EFT_PAYMENT_ACTION_STATEMENT_ID_REQUIRED, EFT_PAYMENT_INVOICE_REVERSE_UNEXPECTED_STATUS, EFT_PAYMENT_ACTION_CREDIT_LINK_STATUS_INVALID, EFT_PAYMENT_ACTION_UNPAID_STATEMENT, EFT_PAYMENT_ACTION_REVERSAL_EXCEEDS_SIXTY_DAYS) on validation failure."},{"name":"EFTService.get_statement_credit_invoice_links","direction":"sends","what":"Called to fetch credit-invoice links for the given short name and statement."},{"name":"EFTService._validate_reversal_credit_invoice_links","direction":"sends","what":"Called to validate link statuses and payment date constraints before reversal."},{"name":"InvoiceModel.find_by_id","direction":"sends","what":"Reads invoice record by id to check invoice_status_code."},{"name":"InvoiceStatus","direction":"reads","what":"Enum with REFUND_REQUESTED, REFUNDED, CANCELLED, PAID values used for status filtering and validation."},{"name":"EFTRefundService.return_eft_credit","direction":"sends","what":"Called for each non-skipped link to create a reversed EFT credit record."},{"name":"EFTCreditInvoiceLinkModel","direction":"sends","what":"New instance created with PENDING_REFUND status, amount, receipt_number, invoice_id, and link_group_id; flushed to database."},{"name":"EFTCreditInvoiceLinkModel.get_next_group_link_seq","direction":"sends","what":"Called to generate the next group link sequence id for all new link records."},{"name":"EFTCreditInvoiceStatus","direction":"reads","what":"Enum with PENDING, PENDING_REFUND, REFUNDED, CANCELLED values used for status checking and link creation."},{"name":"StatementModel.find_by_id","direction":"sends","what":"Reads statement record by id to retrieve payment_account_id and dates."},{"name":"EFTHistoryService.create_statement_reverse","direction":"sends","what":"Called with EFTHistory object containing short_name_id, reversed amount, credit balance, payment_account_id, link_group_id, statement_number, hidden=False, is_processing=True; flushed."},{"name":"EFTCreditModel.get_eft_credit_balance","direction":"sends","what":"Called to retrieve current EFT credit balance for the short name."},{"name":"EftService._send_reversed_payment_notification","direction":"sends","what":"Called with statement and reversed_credits to notify admins."},{"name":"PaymentAccountModel.find_by_id","direction":"sends","what":"Reads payment account by id to get auth_account_id and account name."},{"name":"StatementService.get_summary","direction":"sends","what":"Called with auth_account_id to retrieve summary dict with total_due."},{"name":"StatementService.calculate_due_date","direction":"sends","what":"Called with statement to_date to compute due date."},{"name":"get_account_admin_users","direction":"sends","what":"External call to retrieve account admins; response expected with 'members' list containing admin user contact emails."},{"name":"send_email","direction":"sends","what":"Called with recipients list, subject, rendered body from template, and context kwargs; no retry on failure shown."},{"name":"_render_payment_reversed_template","direction":"sends","what":"Renders email body with email_params dict."},{"name":"EFTCreditInvoiceLinkModel.status_code","direction":"reads","what":"Checked against invalid statuses (PENDING, PENDING_REFUND, REFUNDED) and alt_flow statuses."},{"name":"InvoiceModel.invoice_status_code","direction":"reads","what":"Checked for PAID status; if not PAID (and not in alt_flow list), reversal fails."},{"name":"PaymentMethod.EFT","direction":"reads","what":"Enum value used to filter invoices by payment method in 60-day validation query."},{"name":"db.session.query","direction":"sends","what":"Standard ORM query calls to fetch and aggregate data."},{"name":"current_app.logger","direction":"sends","what":"Logs debug entry/exit and error messages on unexpected invoice status."}]}

42688.text:
{"condensed":"Factory and initialization module for the pay-queue service worker, which applies payments, receipts and account balance to the payment system.

The module exports `create_app(run_mode)`, called by the deployment entry point. It configures a Flask application in the specified `run_mode` (defaults to environment variable `DEPLOYMENT_ENV`, or 'production'). The app loads configuration from `config.CONFIGURATION[run_mode]`. If `SENTRY_DSN` is set in config, it initializes Sentry error tracking with `send_default_pii=False` and release tag `pay-queue@{version}`. It then initializes the GCP queue service, feature flags service, database, and endpoints via `register_endpoints(app)`. Finally it calls `build_cache(app)`.

`build_cache(app)` initializes the cache and clears it. When not in test mode (`TESTING` is False), it attempts to import `CodeService` from `pay_api.services.code` and calls `CodeService.build_all_codes_cache()` to populate the cache. If that call raises any exception, the error is logged but not re-raised; the app continues to start. The module defines no entry points or decision conditions beyond config-driven initialization.","defines":["create_app","build_cache"],"uses":[{"name":"config.CONFIGURATION","direction":"reads","what":"Configuration dict keyed by run_mode string, determines app.config settings"},{"name":"sentry_sdk.init","direction":"sends","what":"Error tracking initialization with DSN, Flask integration, and version tag"},{"name":"queue.init_app","direction":"sends","what":"Initializes GCP queue service with the Flask app"},{"name":"flags.init_app","direction":"sends","what":"Initializes feature flags service with the Flask app"},{"name":"db.init_app","direction":"sends","what":"Initializes database with the Flask app"},{"name":"register_endpoints","direction":"sends","what":"Registers Flask endpoints/routes on the app"},{"name":"cache.init_app","direction":"sends","what":"Initializes cache service with the Flask app"},{"name":"cache.clear","direction":"sends","what":"Clears all cached data"},{"name":"pay_api.services.code.Code.build_all_codes_cache","direction":"sends","what":"Populates the code cache with all codes; called only when TESTING is False; any exception is logged and swallowed"},{"name":"setup_logging","direction":"sends","what":"Configures logging from logging.conf file at module initialization"}]}

42773.text:
{"condensed":"Static configuration for business-filing UI: per-entity-type filing flows, fees, certifications, director warnings, legal obligations and dissolution wording. The aggregator `ConfigJson` holds nine entity types (BC, BEN, CC, ULC with continue-in twins C, CBEN, CCC, CUL; plus CP, GP, SP). Each type specifies entityType, displayName, flows (feeCode, displayName, certifyText, optional warnings), obligations, dissolutionConfirmation and optional todoList. Breadcrumb functions build registry and credential hrefs, initialising the Pinia authenticationStore at module load and appending `?accountid` when present. The route guard requiresAuth: true is set on digital credentials routes only.

Director warnings vary by type: BC/BEN/ULC require minDirectors 1; CC requires 3; CP requires 3 plus bcResident (one) and canadianResident (majority) plus multiCompliance flag. BC, BEN, CC, ULC certify against corporation acts with $5,000 max fine. CP certifies against Cooperative Association Act. GP and SP have no fee, no certifyText, certify against Partnership Act. Spread-based continue-in configs inherit all base content without override mechanism. Dissolution wording: "voluntarily dissolve" for BEN/ULC, "dissolve" for GP/SP.

GOTCHA: Config objects lack interfaces or types; shape is inferred and each carries "FUTURE: needs an interface or type" comment—a typo in flow or warning keys fails silently. GOTCHA: Breadcrumb functions show no null-safety checks. GOTCHA: authenticationStore initialised at BreadcrumbResources.ts module import; if Pinia state unavailable, breadcrumbs may omit account id.","defines":["ConfigJson","Flow","Business","BusinessConfigBc","BusinessConfigBen","BusinessConfigCc","BusinessConfigUlc","BusinessConfigCoop","BusinessConfigPartnership","BusinessConfigSoleProp","BreadcrumbResources","getRegistryDashboardBreadcrumb","getMyBusinessRegistryBreadcrumb","getStaffDashboardBreadcrumb","getDigitalCredentialBreadcrumb","getDashboardBreadcrumb","DigitalCredentialRoutes"],"uses":[{"name":"Pinia authenticationStore","direction":"reads","what":"accountId to append to breadcrumb hrefs when present; state availability at module load time"},{"name":"use-business-dashboard flag","direction":"reads","what":"feature flag controlling whether getDashboardBreadcrumb returns entity href or route name"},{"name":"CredentialsDashboard","direction":"receives","what":"empty route path component for digital credentials area"},{"name":"CredentialsStepper","direction":"receives","what":"route component for ISSUE_CREDENTIAL entry point"},{"name":"BreadcrumbIF","direction":"reads","what":"return type interface for all breadcrumb functions"}]}

42787.text:
{"condensed":"Display-only Vue components for a business dashboard: renders contextual alert panels in priority order (in-dissolution, amalgamation, disable-non-benevolent-corps, frozen-information, missing-information, not-in-compliance, not-in-good-standing) and a dismissible legal-obligation card, both driven by store state flags. No API calls or persistence.

Alerts.vue builds alert list from seven boolean flags in `useBusinessStore`; computed `alerts` maps flags to components, `togglePanel(index)` opens/closes panels (storing open state as index; NaN when closed), and emits `count` on mount and change. InDissolution and Amalgamation extract and format warning dates from store data: Amalgamation finds type `WarningTypes.FUTURE_EFFECTIVE_AMALGAMATION` and formats with `DateUtilities.apiToPacificDate`; InDissolution finds type containing `WarningTypes.INVOLUNTARY_DISSOLUTION`, reads `data.targetDissolutionDate`, converts via `yyyyMmDdToDate` then `dateToPacificDate`, showing 'Unknown' if missing. FrozenInformation and MissingInformation conditionally hide phone numbers: `hidePhoneNumbers = isEntityFirm && !GetFeatureFlag('show-alert-phone-numbers-firm')`, passed as `hidePhoneTollFree`/`hidePhoneVictoria` (FrozenInformation) or `hidePhoneNumbers` (MissingInformation) to shared `ContactInfo` child. CorporateOnline builds description via `GetCorpFullDescription(getLegalType)` and links to `getCorporateOnlineUrl` in new tab. LegalObligation renders only when `showLegalObligation && getObligations && isBusinessWithNoMaintenanceFilings && isBusiness` (where `isBusiness` checks `sessionStorage.BUSINESS_ID`); watcher `@Watch('isActive', {immediate: true})` sets `showLegalObligation` on mount and change; dismiss button sets it false locally (unpersisted); "Read more" toggles detail section. No permission checks shown. Panel header disables pointer events; only details button allows toggle.

GOTCHA: New alert types must be added to Alerts.vue computed property or they never appear and are not counted. GOTCHA: Panel open state stored as index; if alert list changes while open, index may point to wrong alert. GOTCHA: Amalgamation and InDissolution read warning data without guards; missing warning or date could produce wrong/empty result (only InDissolution has 'Unknown' fallback).","defines":["Alerts.vue","InDissolution.vue","Amalgamation.vue","FrozenInformation.vue","MissingInformation.vue","CorporateOnline.vue","LegalObligation.vue","ContactInfo (shared child)","togglePanel","count"],"uses":[{"name":"useBusinessStore","direction":"reads","what":"getBusinessWarnings, isEntityFirm, getCorporateOnlineUrl, getLegalType, getObligations, isInDissolutionAlert, isAmalgamationAlert, isDisableNonBenCorps, isFrozenInformationAlert, isMissingInformationAlert, isNotInComplianceAlert, isNotInGoodStandingAlert, isBusinessWithNoMaintenanceFilings (seven boolean alert flags and data dependencies)"},{"name":"useRootStore","direction":"reads","what":"getCurrentDate"},{"name":"DateUtilities.apiToPacificDate","direction":"sends","what":"called with warning date and true parameter; returns formatted date"},{"name":"yyyyMmDdToDate","direction":"sends","what":"called with target dissolution date string; returns Date object"},{"name":"dateToPacificDate","direction":"sends","what":"called with Date object; returns formatted date string"},{"name":"GetFeatureFlag","direction":"reads","what":"called with 'show-alert-phone-numbers-firm'; returns boolean to control phone number display"},{"name":"GetCorpFullDescription","direction":"sends","what":"called with getLegalType; returns description text for CorporateOnline alert"},{"name":"getCorporateOnlineUrl","direction":"reads","what":"external URL opened in new tab by CorporateOnline alert"},{"name":"sessionStorage.BUSINESS_ID","direction":"reads","what":"checked to determine isBusiness flag; presence indicates business context"},{"name":"WarningTypes.FUTURE_EFFECTIVE_AMALGAMATION","direction":"reads","what":"warning type constant matched to extract amalgamation warning"},{"name":"WarningTypes.INVOLUNTARY_DISSOLUTION","direction":"reads","what":"warning type constant matched (substring) to extract in-dissolution warning"}]}

42873.text:
{"condensed":"Vue frontend for business filings, entity header/menu, and dashboard in BC Registries. Views read `filingId` from `$route.query` (0 for new, >0 for draft); load drafts via `LegalServices.fetchFiling('businesses/{identifier}/filings/{filingId}')` and save through `createFiling` or `updateFiling(identifier, filing, filingId, isDraft)`. Filing body contains `header` (name, certifiedBy, email, date, FilingTypes.*), `business` (foundingDate, identifier, legalName, legalType), and filing-specific block (annualReport, changeOfDirectors, etc.). Staff payment adds routingSlipNumber (FAS), bcolAccountNumber/datNumber/folioNumber (BCOL), or waiveFees (NO_FEE). Fee codes push through `updateFilingData(...)` to `SbcFeeSummary` returning `totalFee`. On success with `isPaymentActionRequired`, navigates to `getAuthWebUrl + 'makepayment/' + paymentToken + '/' + returnUrl`; otherwise to dashboard. `AmalgamationSelection.vue` calls `createBusinessAA(type)` → `LegalServices.createDraftBusiness(...)` with `amalgamationApplication` draft, routes to `amalg-short-information` or `amalg-reg-information?id=businessId`, throws 'Invalid business identifier' if no identifier. `Signin.vue` redirects to `getLoginUrl?return=<encoded sessionStorage BASE_URL>`; `Signout.vue` wraps SbcSignout.

`isPageValid` gates File and Pay, combining per-section flags. `isPayRequired` is `totalFee > 0`. Staff detour: `onClickFilePay` opens Staff Payment dialog when `isRoleStaff && !fromStaffPayment` (AnnualReport, ConsentAmalgamationOut, ConsentContinuationOut, StandaloneDirectorsFiling, StandaloneOfficeAddressFiling). `busySaving` blocks double clicks. `saveFiling(isDraft)` builds filing; errors store `response.data.errors`/`warnings` in `saveErrors`/`saveWarnings` then re-raise. 402 clears `haveChanges`, opens `paymentErrorDialog`, keeps filing; `onPaymentErrorDialogExit` goes to dashboard unless `isRoleStaff`. Other errors set `saveErrorReason` (SAVE, SAVE_RESUME, FILE_PAY); dialogs retry or finish. `goToDashboard(force)` shows 'Unsaved Changes' confirm when `haveChanges` true. Draft restore checks filing type, status DRAFT, matching identifier; failure opens `resumeErrorDialog`. Staff-only views throw if `!isRoleStaff`. AGM Extension prevents draft resume (filingId !== 0). AGM Location Change limits year to currentYear−2…+1, location to 400 chars. AnnualReport.mounted validates identifier, year, filingId; requires `arMinDate`/`arMaxDate` (coop) or `nextARDate` (BC); failure calls `goToDashboard(true)`. AnnualReport.allowChange checks AGM date. EntityMenu: change-business-info and dissolve return false when `!isGoodStanding && !isRoleStaff`, else disabled unless `isAllowed(...)` passes; filtered by feature flags and entity type. DigitalCredentials.mounted redirects unless `isAllowed(DIGITAL_CREDENTIALS)`. Dashboard buttons disabled by `isAllowed(ADDRESS_CHANGE)` and `isAllowed(DIRECTOR_CHANGE)`. `onAddressChangeClick` branches on firm (edit), base company (COA warning), or other (standalone).

GOTCHA: pay-URL `navigate()` unguarded; failure strands user; 402 sets `haveChanges=false` unconditionally. GOTCHA: EntityMenu references commented-out `isEntityCoop` and `isEntityFirm` getters; may fail at runtime. GOTCHA: client-side role checks (created throwing, mounted redirect) only gate shown; no server-side check appears. GOTCHA: `window.onbeforeunload` overwritten without saving previous handler. GOTCHA: `StandaloneOfficeAddressFiling` hardcodes `email: 'no_one@never.get'`.","defines":["AnnualReport.vue","AgmExtension.vue","AgmLocationChange.vue","AmalgamationSelection.vue","AmalgamationOut.vue","ChangeOfDirectors.vue","ChangeOfAddress.vue","ConsentAmalgamationOut.vue","ConsentContinuationOut.vue","ContinuationOut.vue","StandaloneDirectorsFiling.vue","StandaloneOfficeAddressFiling.vue","DigitalCredentials.vue","EntityMenu.vue","EntityHeader.vue","Dashboard.vue","Signin.vue","Signout.vue","isPageValid","isPayRequired","saveFiling(isDraft)","goToDashboard(force)","fetchDraftFiling","onClickFilePay","onPaymentErrorDialogExit","onSaveErrorDialogRetry","onSaveErrorDialogOkay","onAddressChangeClick","allowChange","createBusinessAA(type)"],"uses":[{"name":"LegalServices.fetchFiling('businesses/{identifier}/filings/{filingId}')","direction":"sends","what":"GET request to fetch draft filing by business identifier and filing ID; returns filing body with header, business, and type-specific block"},{"name":"LegalServices.createFiling","direction":"sends","what":"POST to create new filing (filingId 0); sends header, business, and filing-specific block; returns filing with filingId"},{"name":"LegalServices.updateFiling(identifier, filing, filingId, isDraft)","direction":"sends","what":"POST/PUT to save draft or submit filing; sends full filing body; returns updated filing"},{"name":"LegalServices.hasPendingTasks(identifier)","direction":"sends","what":"GET to check for pending tasks before creating new filing; called before createFiling"},{"name":"LegalServices.createDraftBusiness(...)","direction":"sends","what":"POST to create draft business for amalgamation application; sends type (PRIMARY/HOLDING/AMALGAMATING) and amalgationApplication block; returns business with identifier"},{"name":"SbcFeeSummary","direction":"receives","what":"receives fee codes (FilingCodes.*) via updateFilingData(...); returns totalFee"},{"name":"updateFilingData(...)","direction":"sends","what":"sends fee codes to SbcFeeSummary and receives totalFee back"},{"name":"getAuthWebUrl + 'makepayment/' + paymentToken","direction":"sends","what":"navigates user to payment URL when isPaymentActionRequired and totalFee > 0; includes returnUrl with filing_id query param"},{"name":"getLoginUrl","direction":"reads","what":"URL for sign-in redirection with return=<encoded sessionStorage BASE_URL> in Signin.vue; used by Signout.vue as redirect"},{"name":"sessionStorage BASE_URL","direction":"reads","what":"base URL stored in session storage; encoded and passed to getLoginUrl"},{"name":"SbcSignout","direction":"receives","what":"component wrapped by Signout.vue; passed getLoginUrl as redirect prop"},{"name":"$route.query.filingId","direction":"reads","what":"query parameter read from route; 0 for new filing, >0 for draft to resume"},{"name":"isRoleStaff","direction":"reads","what":"boolean flag determining if user has staff role; gates staff-payment dialog and staff-only views"},{"name":"isGoodStanding","direction":"reads","what":"boolean flag; EntityMenu returns false for change-business-info and dissolve when false unless isRoleStaff"},{"name":"isAllowed(...)","direction":"reads","what":"permission check function; gates EntityMenu items, ADDRESS_CHANGE, DIRECTOR_CHANGE, DIGITAL_CREDENTIALS; no check shown in this chunk"},{"name":"FilingTypes.*","direction":"reads","what":"enumeration of filing type names in header"},{"name":"FilingCodes.*","direction":"reads","what":"fee code constants pushed to SbcFeeSummary"},{"name":"currentYear","direction":"reads","what":"current year; used to limit AGM Location Change year range to currentYear−2…+1"},{"name":"arMinDate, arMaxDate, nextARDate","direction":"reads","what":"date bounds for annual report validation; arMinDate/arMaxDate for coop, nextARDate for BC"},{"name":"isEntityCoop, isEntityFirm","direction":"reads","what":"entity type getters referenced by EntityMenu but commented out; may fail at runtime"},{"name":"response.data.errors, response.data.warnings","direction":"receives","what":"error and warning arrays from save/file responses; stored in saveErrors and saveWarnings"},{"name":"saveErrorReason","direction":"reads","what":"stores error type (SAVE, SAVE_RESUME, FILE_PAY) to determine retry/finish action"},{"name":"window.onbeforeunload","direction":"sends","what":"overwritten without saving previous handler for unsaved changes detection"}]}

