{"condensed":"Pytest unit test suite for the pay-api payment service, running against a test database and mocking all external calls (CFS/PayBC, Notify, Keycloak, GCP Pub/Sub, LaunchDarkly, report service). Contains no production code.

Tests pin payment system selection: CC routes to Paybc or InternalPay (zero fees or staff), DIRECT_PAY to DirectPay, DRAWDOWN to Bcol, EFT to Eft, PAD to Pad; PAD blocks until confirmation period passes, invalid corp/filing raises exception. Auth check raises 403 on missing roles. Blockers reject NSF (PAD) and overdue (EFT) invoices. Invoice creation starts as SETTLEMENT_SCHEDULED or COMPLETED (zero amount), deducts from routing slip remaining, soft-deletes cascade payment, rolls back on exception with ServiceUnavailableException. Failed-payment retry consolidates multiple failures into new invoice with sum amount and tracks cons_inv_number. Transaction updates fail on invalid invoice/transaction or missing receipt; DIRECT_PAY hash validated; connection error yields FAILED; queue failure yields EVENT_FAILED; NSF/EFT completion clears flags and reactivates account. Refunds fail for unpaid/duplicate invoices; status depends on method (PAD/ONLINE_BANKING/CC→CREDITED, DRAWDOWN/DIRECT_PAY→REFUND_REQUESTED); PAD APPROVED→CANCELLED; DirectPay rejects PayBC mismatch/excess/already-refunded. EFT credit refund/reversal validates balance; process_cfs_refund handles six scenarios updating link/remaining/history, rejects consolidated invoices. Payment accounts: EFT overrides PAD, future PAD falls back to DRAWDOWN; deletion blocked by outstanding credit/frozen/in-progress. Statement switch to/from EFT creates settings (EFT→MONTHLY, DRAWDOWN→WEEKLY) and may generate interim. Routing slip link sets child LINKED with zero remaining, parent remaining sums children. FeeSchedule applies priority/future-effective/waive/service fees. Business-day calc skips holidays/weekends. BCOL/OAuth map error codes; OAuth converts connection errors to ServiceUnavailableException.

GOTCHA: `test_fee_schedule_with_service_fees_for_basic_user` expects service_fees=10 with `include_service_fees=False`, suggesting flag has no effect. GOTCHA: `test_cfs_service` expects HTTP 400 invalid-bank-account to report status_code 200, masking upstream error. GOTCHA: Several tests assert only that something returned (payment_system_service asserts exception occurred); EFT refund tests do not verify `save` called.","defines":["tests/conftest.py","emails_with_keycloak_role_mock","send_email_mock","test_email_service.py","test_gcp_queue.py","factory_payment_account","factory_invoice","PaymentSystemFactory.create","PaymentSystemFactory.create_from_payment_method","check_auth","ensure_no_payment_blockers","PaymentService.create_invoice","PaymentService.delete_invoice","create_account_payment","PaymentTransactionService.create_transaction_for_invoice","PaymentTransactionService.update_transaction","HashingService","RefundService.create_refund","REFUND_SUCCESS_MESSAGES","refund_eft_credits","reverse_eft_credits","process_cfs_refund","PaymentAccountService.create","PaymentAccountService.update","PaymentAccountService.delete_account","update_statement_settings","get_statement_report","do_link","FeeSchedule.find_by_corp_type_and_filing_type","get_nearest_business_day","get_bcol_error","OAuthService","test_payment_service.py","test_payment_transaction.py","test_payment_system_factory.py"],"uses":[{"name":"get_emails_with_keycloak_role","direction":"receives","what":"Patched in pay_api.services.auth and pay_api.services.eft_refund; returns 'hello@goodnight.com' in tests."},{"name":"send_email","direction":"receives","what":"Patched in email_service and eft_refund; returns True in tests."},{"name":"OAuthService.post","direction":"sends","what":"Called with NOTIFY_API_ENDPOINT, bearer service-account token, JSON payload {recipients, content:{subject, body}}; returns True when notifyStatus is SUCCESS."},{"name":"NOTIFY_API_ENDPOINT","direction":"reads","what":"Config key for Notify API endpoint used by email_service."},{"name":"GcpQueue.publish","direction":"sends","what":"Called with topic and message; skips when topic is None."},{"name":"freeze_time","direction":"reads","what":"Test utility used in some tests."},{"name":"skip_in_pod","direction":"reads","what":"Test utility used in some tests."},{"name":"PAD_CONFIRMATION_PERIOD_IN_DAYS","direction":"reads","what":"Config constant for PAD confirmation period blocking threshold."},{"name":"ACCOUNT_IN_PAD_CONFIRMATION_PERIOD","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised when PAD confirmation period has not passed."},{"name":"INVALID_CORP_OR_FILING_TYPE","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised for invalid corp or filing type."},{"name":"SETTLEMENT_SCHEDULED","direction":"reads","what":"Invoice status constant used on creation."},{"name":"COMPLETED","direction":"reads","what":"Invoice status constant for zero-amount and fully-deducted invoices."},{"name":"ServiceUnavailableException","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised on connection errors during invoice creation and OAuth calls."},{"name":"INVALID_PAYMENT_METHOD","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised when EFT flag is off."},{"name":"INVALID_INVOICE_ID","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised when transaction invoice is invalid."},{"name":"COMPLETED_PAYMENT","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised when attempting transaction on completed payment."},{"name":"INVALID_TRANSACTION","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised when updating non-existent transaction."},{"name":"FAILED","direction":"reads","what":"Transaction status for missing receipt, bad DIRECT_PAY hash, or connection error."},{"name":"EVENT_FAILED","direction":"reads","what":"Transaction status when queue publish fails."},{"name":"has_nsf_invoices","direction":"reads","what":"Account flag cleared on NSF payment completion."},{"name":"has_overdue_invoices","direction":"reads","what":"Account flag cleared on EFT payment completion."},{"name":"CFS account reactivation","direction":"sends","what":"Account reactivated on NSF payment completion."},{"name":"CREDITED","direction":"reads","what":"Refund status for PAD, ONLINE_BANKING, CC methods."},{"name":"REFUND_REQUESTED","direction":"reads","what":"Refund status for DRAWDOWN and DIRECT_PAY methods."},{"name":"CANCELLED","direction":"reads","what":"Refund status for PAD APPROVED invoices; refund_date set."},{"name":"REFUNDED","direction":"reads","what":"Refund status; refund_date set."},{"name":"refund_date","direction":"reads","what":"Field set for CANCELLED, CREDITED, REFUNDED refunds."},{"name":"DIRECT_PAY_INVALID_RESPONSE","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised on PayBC HTTPError or approved=0 for DirectPay refunds."},{"name":"build_automated_refund_payload","direction":"reads","what":"Function rejecting PayBC mismatch, excess amount, already-refunded with INVALID_REQUEST."},{"name":"INVALID_REQUEST","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised by refund payload builder."},{"name":"INVALID_REFUND","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised when EFT credit amount exceeds balance or reversal has leftover/excess."},{"name":"INVALID_CONSOLIDATED_REFUND","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised when processing consolidated invoice refund."},{"name":"EFTHistory","direction":"reads","what":"Table updated by process_cfs_refund with six scenarios."},{"name":"remaining_amount","direction":"reads","what":"Field on invoice and EFT link tracking available balance."},{"name":"link status","direction":"reads","what":"Field updated by process_cfs_refund scenarios."},{"name":"OUTSTANDING_CREDIT","direction":"reads","what":"Exception blocking account deletion."},{"name":"FROZEN_ACCOUNT","direction":"reads","what":"Exception blocking account deletion."},{"name":"TRANSACTIONS_IN_PROGRESS","direction":"reads","what":"Exception blocking account deletion."},{"name":"MONTHLY","direction":"reads","what":"Statement setting when switching to EFT."},{"name":"WEEKLY","direction":"reads","what":"Statement setting when switching to DRAWDOWN."},{"name":"ReportService","direction":"sends","what":"Called to build PDF for get_statement_report."},{"name":"LINKED","direction":"reads","what":"Routing slip status set by do_link on child slip."},{"name":"BusinessException","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised by ensure_no_payment_blockers."},{"name":"cons_inv_number","direction":"reads","what":"Field set on old payments in failed-payment consolidation."},{"name":"invoice_amount","direction":"reads","what":"Field set to sum of consolidated failed payments."},{"name":"BC and Canadian holidays","direction":"reads","what":"Dates skipped by get_nearest_business_day."},{"name":"Keycloak","direction":"reads","what":"Mocked auth service; provides get_emails_with_keycloak_role."},{"name":"PayBC/CFS","direction":"sends","what":"Mocked external payment gateway; called for payment processing."},{"name":"GCP Pub/Sub","direction":"sends","what":"Mocked message queue; publish_to_queue publishes QueueMessage."},{"name":"LaunchDarkly","direction":"reads","what":"Mocked feature flag service."},{"name":"HTTPException","direction":"reads","what":"Exception raised by check_auth on auth failure."},{"name":"one_of_roles","direction":"reads","what":"Auth check parameter."},{"name":"contains_role","direction":"reads","what":"Auth check parameter."}]}

42916.text:
{"condensed":"Flask REST layer serving business filings, addresses, parties, documents and digital credentials with invoice creation, NATS events and Minio storage.

Entry points: `@jwt.requires_auth` on most routes; internal routes need `UserRoles.colin`, `UserRoles.system` or `SYSTEM_ROLE`. Filing JSON validated against `filing` schema, 400 on error. POST filing saves it, creates invoice via `PAYMENT_SVC_URL` (stores `payment_token`, `payment_status_code`, `payment_account`). Publishes: `{filing.id}` for COLIN filings to queue; `bc.registry.bnmove` `{oldBn,newBn}` and `bc.registry.business.bn` to NATS topics. Decisions: POST filing requires type in `CoreFiling.NEW_BUSINESS_FILING_TYPES` (400); `RegistrationBootstrapService` needed (503). GET: `slim=true` slim response; `allowed_filings=true` adds allowed filings; `accountId` only for system/account-identity JWTs. `/search` (SYSTEM_ROLE only): empty `identifiers` list is 400; drafts are filings with `temp_reg` and no business. `ListFilingResource.check_authorization` requires both `authorized(edit)` and `is_allowed(...)` pass (401). Validation skipped for `query.draft`, COLIN source before `BOB_DATE`, or `is_before_epoch_filing`. `complete_filing`: COLIN goes to `process_colin_filing` (needs `colin_event_ids`); else runs `check_and_update_nr`, `set_effective_date`, `get_filing_types`, `create_invoice` (402 on payment 400, connection error or timeout). Change-requested filing goes to `resubmit_filing_for_review`, sets Review RESUBMITTED. Filing DELETE: locked filings refused; deletes Minio files and bootstrap for `T`. PATCH: DELETE payment token; 200/202 calls `reset_filing_to_draft`. Document delete only when `is_draft_filing` (403). Digital credentials: `@can_access_digital_credentials` required. `create_invitation`: 409 if active connection exists, reuses pending invitation. `send_credential`: 500 if credential exchange id set. `revoke_credential`: reason SELF_REISSUANCE or SELF_REVOCATION via `reissue` flag. Webhook `/topic/<name>`: `connections` sets active on ACTIVE/COMPLETED; `issuer_cred_rev` records revocation ids when state `issued`; `issue_credential_v2_0` sets `is_issued` when state `done`. Furnishing: staff/system only, 404 for GAZETTE, variant `default`/`greyscale`. Colin sync: `GET /internal/filings` skips corrections without `ColinEventId`, involuntary dissolutions without `BatchProcessing`, amalgamations that raise; PATCH appends `ColinEventId`. `bnmove` updates `tax_id`, creates registrarsNotation filing, publishes events. Tasks: non-consumable Name Request gives 403.

GOTCHA: No permission check on document GET/DELETE, `business.py` GET, `business_tasks`, `save_filing`. Digital credentials webhook has no check. GOTCHA: `bnmove` returns 200 even when business missing or filing creation fails; no null-check or rollback. GOTCHA: PATCH cancel resets filing to DRAFT regardless of payment DELETE response. GOTCHA: `DCConnection` saved before invitation call finishes, leaving orphaned rows. GOTCHA: `construct_task_list` returns string `'pay_connection_error'` instead of list. GOTCHA: `update_colin_event_id` uses raw SQL with f-string.","defines":["business_filings POST","business_filings GET","/search","business_filings DELETE","business_filings PATCH","business_filings/{id}","ListFilingResource.check_authorization","complete_filing","resubmit_filing_for_review","reset_filing_to_draft","create_invoice","check_and_update_nr","set_effective_date","get_filing_types","process_colin_filing","document DELETE","document GET","create_signed_put_url","create_signed_get_url","digital_credentials/create_invitation","digital_credentials/send_credential","digital_credentials/revoke_credential","/topic/<name>","DCConnection","DCConnection.find_active_by","DCConnection.find_by_connection_id","DCConnection.find_by","furnishing_document POST","/internal/filings GET","/internal/filings PATCH","bnmove","business_tasks","RegistrationBootstrapService"],"uses":[{"name":"@jwt.requires_auth","direction":"receives","what":"Authentication decorator; most routes require valid JWT token"},{"name":"authorized","direction":"receives","what":"Permission check function called with identifier, JWT and action list; must pass else 401"},{"name":"UserRoles.colin","direction":"reads","what":"Role constant for internal COLIN routes"},{"name":"UserRoles.system","direction":"reads","what":"Role constant for internal system routes"},{"name":"SYSTEM_ROLE","direction":"reads","what":"Role constant for internal system routes"},{"name":"rsbc_schemas.validate","direction":"sends","what":"Validates filing JSON against filing schema; returns errors with 400"},{"name":"PAYMENT_SVC_URL","direction":"sends","what":"POST creates invoice with filing data; sends Bearer JWT; returns payment token, status code and account; 402 on 400, connection error or timeout"},{"name":"NATS_EMAILER_SUBJECT","direction":"sends","what":"Publishes bc.registry.bnmove event with oldBn and newBn"},{"name":"NATS_ENTITY_EVENT_SUBJECT","direction":"sends","what":"Publishes bc.registry.business.bn event"},{"name":"queue","direction":"sends","what":"Publishes {filing.id} for COLIN-source filings"},{"name":"CoreFiling.NEW_BUSINESS_FILING_TYPES","direction":"reads","what":"List of allowed filing types for new business; else 400"},{"name":"BOB_DATE","direction":"reads","what":"Cutoff date for COLIN historical filings; before this skips validation"},{"name":"Minio","direction":"sends","what":"Deletes draft filing documents; creates signed PUT URLs (5-minute) and GET URLs (1-hour) with UUID keys"},{"name":"@can_access_digital_credentials","direction":"receives","what":"Authorization decorator for digital credential routes"},{"name":"DCConnection","direction":"reads","what":"Model storing connection_id, invitation_url, is_active, connection_state and business_id; state progresses init→invitation→request→response→active→completed"},{"name":"digital_credentials service","direction":"sends","what":"Calls create_invitation, send_credential, revoke_credential endpoints"},{"name":"/topic/<name> webhook","direction":"receives","what":"Unauthenticated webhook receiving connection, revocation and credential events with no permission check"},{"name":"ColinEventId","direction":"reads","what":"Column identifying Colin sync records; corrections and involuntary dissolutions skipped without it"},{"name":"BatchProcessing","direction":"reads","what":"Table row required for involuntary dissolution sync"},{"name":"Namex","direction":"sends","what":"Called by check_and_update_nr for Name Request processing"},{"name":"is_allowed","direction":"receives","what":"Permission check that must pass along with authorized for filing list access, else 401"},{"name":"tax_id","direction":"sends","what":"Updated in bnmove operation"},{"name":"filing schema","direction":"reads","what":"JSON validation schema; errors returned as {errors} with 400"}]}

43146.text:
{"condensed":"Documentation and fixtures for the PayBC mock API (BC government CFS payment provider), defined as OpenAPI 3.0 YAML. It specifies endpoints and message shapes that the mock service implements and that clients are tested against. Callers consume these shapes; the documentation hands work to nothing.

Core endpoints: Refund (`POST /paybc-service/api/refund`, takes `RefundRequest` with `orderNumber`, `pbcRefNumber`, `txnAmount`, `txnNumber`, returns `RefundResponse` with `id`, `approved`, `amount`, `message`, `created`, `orderNumber`, `txnNumber`; documented statuses 200, 201, 401, 403, 404). Payment query returns transaction fields and `revenue[]` array with GL status and optional `refund_data[]` per line, plus top-level `postedrefundamount` and `refundedamount`. Receipts (`Rcpt` schema) support create, list, get, update, and apply-to-invoices (`POST .../rcpts/{receipt_number}/apply` with `invoice_info`, returns `Rcpt`). Invoices support create, get, update; adjustment creation is truncated. Credit balance `POST /cfs/parties/invs/{inv_number}/creditbalance/` returns `Inv` with `credit_memo`. Bank validation `POST /cfs/validatepayins/` takes `Bank_info`, returns bank fields plus `CAS-Returned-Messages` (VALID or error codes like "0001 - Bank Number is Invalid"); 400 returns `ErrorResponse`. All paths hang off `/cfs/parties/{party_number}/accs/{account_number}/sites/{site_number}/...`. Failures return 400 with `ErrorResponse`. No authorization, validation or lock checks are shown; bank validation outcomes are in `CAS-Returned-Messages` string, not status code. Static YAML fixtures mock receipts `123451`, `123452`, `123453`, and `rcpt_info1/2/3`.

GOTCHA: Examples are inconsistent (receipt_amount as `10.02` or `'$10.02'`; `amount_to_apply` as `'$9.5'`; receipt_date formats vary). GOTCHA: `RefundRequest.txnAmount` is integer while receipt amounts are decimals; cents can be lost. GOTCHA: Truncated definitions (adjustment, receipt list/apply, payment, receipt update) leave implementations guessing at shapes.","defines":["POST /paybc-service/api/refund (refundUsingPOST)","POST .../rcpts/ (Rcpts_POST)","GET .../rcpts/ (Rcpts list)","GET .../rcpts/{receipt_number}/ (Rcpt_GET)","PUT .../rcpts/{receipt_number}/ (Rcpts_PUT)","POST .../rcpts/{receipt_number}/apply (Rcpts_Apply_POST)","POST .../invs/ (Invs_POST)","GET .../invs/{invoice_number}/ (Inv_GET)","PUT .../invs/{invoice_number}/ (Invs_PUT)","POST .../invs/{invoice_number}/adjs/ (adjustment create)","POST /cfs/parties/invs/{inv_number}/creditbalance/","POST .../payment/ (PaymentDetails)","PUT .../accs/ (Accs_PUT)","PUT .../conts/{contact_number}/ (Conts_PUT)","POST /cfs/validatepayins/ (bank validation)","RefundRequest","RefundResponse","ErrorResponse","TokenResponse","Rcpt","Inv","PaymentDetails","Acc","Cont","Party","Link","Bank_info"],"uses":[{"name":"paybc-1.0.0.yaml","direction":"reads","what":"OpenAPI 3.0 specification file defining the complete PayBC contract, including refund, receipt, invoice, bank validation and payment paths and schemas."},{"name":"CAS-Returned-Messages","direction":"reads","what":"Response field from bank validation and credit balance endpoints containing validation outcome codes (VALID or error codes such as '0001 - Bank Number is Invalid') or SUCCESS."},{"name":"Static YAML fixtures (rcpt_info1/2/3, receipts 123451/123452/123453)","direction":"reads","what":"Mock response examples used in tests and by the mock service to generate responses."}]}

43150.text:
{"condensed":"Vue front-end for staff reviewing business continuation-in applications: a searchable, filterable table of reviews; detail sections displaying jurisdiction, registration, correspondence history and review outcome; and a form to submit approval/rejection with optional email body. Reads from BusinessService (searchReviews, downloadDocument). Caches filters and pagination in session storage. Emits review outcome and email text to parent; parent calls validate() before submit.

Search triggers on any filter change (debounced): status, date ranges (creation and effective), NR number, identifier, completing party, sort. Results show NR expiry via orange (≤14 days) or red (expired); effective dates show orange if ≤3 days remain. Row actions: view detail or "Open Name Request" (if NR set). Review outcome requires status code; email body required only for CHANGE_REQUESTED or REJECTED. Previous correspondence assembles history from creation date plus result entries (CHANGE_REQUESTED → "Change Requested" + "Application Resubmitted" if submissionDate exists; APPROVED → "Application Approved"; REJECTED → "Application Rejected"). Jurisdiction resolved via CanJurisdictions, UsaJurisdiction, IntlJurisdictions lookups. All dates shown in America/Vancouver timezone; date picker caps start at end-date or today, end at today (both computed in Vancouver time). Custom date-range presets: TODAY, YESTERDAY, LASTWEEK (isoWeek), LASTMONTH.

GOTCHA: search error caught and logged only; no user message or retry. GOTCHA: no auth/permission check in any component. GOTCHA: DateRangeFilter.dateClick hard-codes index 4 instead of DATEFILTER_CODES.CUSTOMRANGE; reordering presets breaks custom selection. GOTCHA: TestimonialQuotes setInterval never cleared; each mount leaks a timer. GOTCHA: DateMixin.dateToPacificDate has no null/invalid-date handling. Also: PPRLauncher renders card to ConfigHelper.getPPRWebUrl() filtered by currentUser.roles; TestimonialQuotes rotates one hard-coded quote.","defines":["ContinuationApplicationTable.vue","ReviewResult.vue","PreviousCorrespondence.vue","HomeJurisdictionInformation.vue","ExtraprovincialRegistrationBc.vue","DatePicker.vue","DateRangeFilter.vue","DateMixin.dateToPacificDate","DateMixin.strToPacificDate","DateMixin.strToPacificDateTime","PPRLauncher.vue","TestimonialQuotes.vue","review-result event","email-body-text event","validate() method"],"uses":[{"name":"BusinessService.searchReviews","direction":"sends","what":"ReviewFilterParams (startDate, endDate, startEffectiveDate, endEffectiveDate, nrNumber, identifier, completingParty, status[], sortBy, sortDesc, page, limit); returns ContinuationReviewIF[] with totalItemsCount."},{"name":"BusinessService.downloadDocument","direction":"sends","what":"fileKey and fileName; on failure logs to console and opens ModalDialog 'Unable to download document'."},{"name":"CanJurisdictions","direction":"reads","what":"Lookup table for resolving home jurisdiction."},{"name":"UsaJurisdiction","direction":"reads","what":"Lookup table for USA jurisdiction resolution."},{"name":"IntlJurisdictions","direction":"reads","what":"Lookup table for international jurisdiction resolution."},{"name":"moment","direction":"reads","what":"Date library for isoWeek, date arithmetic and timezone operations."},{"name":"session storage keys","direction":"reads","what":"ReviewSearchFilter, ReviewPaginationNumberOfItems, ReviewPaginationOptions supplied by ContinuationApplications.vue."},{"name":"currentUser.roles","direction":"reads","what":"User roles determining PPRLauncher card content (ppr+mhr, mhr only, or ppr)."},{"name":"ConfigHelper.getPPRWebUrl","direction":"sends","what":"Called by PPRLauncher to get URL based on currentUser.roles."},{"name":"goToNameXUI","direction":"sends","what":"Called when 'Open Name Request' is clicked if item.nrNumber is set."},{"name":"ModalDialog","direction":"sends","what":"Opened with title 'Unable to download document' on download failure."}]}

