{"condensed":"FAS routing slips management in pay-api: handles creation, linking, status transitions, refunds and reporting of financial routing slips via `/api/v1/fas/routing-slips` endpoints.

**Entry points:** Create (needs FAS_CREATE, FAS_SEARCH) writes PaymentAccount, CfsAccount (PENDING), RoutingSlip (ACTIVE, remaining_amount=total), Payment rows (COMPLETED, is_routing_slip=True), commits, returns 201. Link child to parent (POST /links, after _validate_linking) raises RS_* errors (RS_ALREADY_LINKED, RS_CHILD_HAS_TRANSACTIONS) as 400 with type code; do_link moves child's remaining_amount to parent, sets child LINKED with 0, commits. Update status (PATCH UPDATE_STATUS) validates via STATUS_TRANSITIONS table; disallowed raises FAS_INVALID_RS_STATUS_CHANGE. _check_roles_for_status_update requires FAS_VOID, FAS_CORRECTION or FAS_REFUND_APPROVER per target. NSF negates children's totals into remaining_amount; VOID blocked if invoices exist, zeroes remaining_amount; CORRECTION recalculates total, may return to ACTIVE or COMPLETE. Four-eyes rule: requester cannot authorize own refund/write-off. Refund flow: ACTIVE→REFUND_REQUESTED (stores mailingAddress in refund.details, returns 202), different user with FAS_REFUND_APPROVER moves to REFUND_AUTHORIZED or WRITE_OFF_AUTHORIZED; can cancel or reject (returns to ACTIVE). Comments: create raises FAS_INVALID_ROUTING_SLIP_NUMBER for missing slip, flushes, commits. Search takes filter/page/limit, returns {total, page, limit, items} via RoutingSlipSchema. find_by_number adds allowedStatuses. create_daily_reports selects by dateFilter, excludes VOID, totals cash/cheque counts and USD/CAD amounts, posts to REPORT_API_BASE_URL via OAuthService.post.

**GOTCHA:** No locking or rollback around multi-record changes (NSF reversal sums children unguarded, do_link and create lack duplicate-submit guard). Transition rules in STATUS_TRANSITIONS table, CORRECTION branch, seeded codes, and per-role tests can drift. Migration 7aff4af4be85 downgrade resets every COMPLETE slip with remaining_amount < 0.01 to ACTIVE, including already-COMPLETE slips. parent_id → parent_number migration shows no data copy; existing links may be lost. CFS call sequences non-atomic, no stated idempotency; mid-sequence failure leaves local and CFS state out of step.","defines":["POST /api/v1/fas/routing-slips","POST /links","PATCH UPDATE_STATUS","RoutingSlip.create","RoutingSlip.update","RoutingSlipStatusTransitionService.validate_possible_transitions","CommentService.create","RoutingSlipSchema","find_by_number","create_daily_reports","get_links","get_possible_transitions","find_all_comments_for_a_routingslip","search","do_link","STATUS_TRANSITIONS","refunds","routing_slip_status_codes","error_codes"],"uses":[{"name":"OAuthService.post","direction":"sends","what":"Posts daily report totals (cash/cheque counts, USD/CAD amounts) to REPORT_API_BASE_URL with OAuth credentials."},{"name":"REPORT_API_BASE_URL","direction":"sends","what":"External report API endpoint receives daily routing slip reports."},{"name":"CFS_API","direction":"sends","what":"Called for receipts, invoices and adjustments during routing slip operations (sequences non-atomic, no stated idempotency)."},{"name":"pay-api database","direction":"sends","what":"Writes PaymentAccount, CfsAccount, RoutingSlip, Payment, refunds, comments rows; reads STATUS_TRANSITIONS, routing_slip_status_codes, error_codes."},{"name":"ALLOW_LEGACY_ROUTING_SLIPS","direction":"reads","what":"Config flag; when set, bypasses 9-digit checksum validation in validate_and_find_by_number."},{"name":"FAS_CREATE","direction":"receives","what":"Permission required to call create endpoint."},{"name":"FAS_SEARCH","direction":"receives","what":"Permission required to call create endpoint."},{"name":"FAS_VOID","direction":"receives","what":"Permission required to authorize VOID status transition."},{"name":"FAS_CORRECTION","direction":"receives","what":"Permission required to authorize CORRECTION status transition."},{"name":"FAS_REFUND_APPROVER","direction":"receives","what":"Permission required to authorize refund/write-off transitions and approve refund requests."}]}
